1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,100
[The D Dorm]

2
00:00:04,830 --> 00:00:06,640
Your wound has dried up.

3
00:00:06,660 --> 00:00:08,780
- Ow...
- You don't need a Band-Aid anymore.

4
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:09,830
By the way...

5
00:00:10,320 --> 00:00:11,300
does it still hurt?

6
00:00:12,130 --> 00:00:12,890
Ow, hey!

7
00:00:21,670 --> 00:00:23,620
Your eyes meet...

8
00:00:23,630 --> 00:00:25,540
gazing at each other.

9
00:00:25,540 --> 00:00:27,250
Something sensual.

10
00:00:27,250 --> 00:00:28,240
Sensual...

11
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:30,040
Sensual, sensual...

12
00:00:33,710 --> 00:00:34,710
When will you let go?

13
00:00:34,730 --> 00:00:35,580
Oh...

14
00:00:40,180 --> 00:00:41,120
You're so weak.

15
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:43,060
That was just a small poke,
but you yelped like you were crushed.

16
00:00:44,170 --> 00:00:45,370
What kind of sane person

17
00:00:45,550 --> 00:00:46,900
pokes other people's wounds?

18
00:00:47,030 --> 00:00:48,300
Is your hand even clean?

19
00:00:48,980 --> 00:00:50,550
Just know that it's cleaner than your mouth.

20
00:00:51,560 --> 00:00:53,410
Don't ask me to
tend your wounds next time, then.

21
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:55,990
Come on...

22
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:56,630
Oh,

23
00:00:56,940 --> 00:00:57,980
by the way...

24
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:00,650
you two seem to get along well.

25
00:01:00,950 --> 00:01:02,960
You bicker back and forth.

26
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:04,700
They say couples like you

27
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:05,770
end up having a bunch of kids.

28
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:06,660
Be quiet,

29
00:01:06,660 --> 00:01:07,310
Grandpa.

30
00:01:07,310 --> 00:01:08,170
Be quiet about what?

31
00:01:08,820 --> 00:01:10,630
I haven't said anything yet,
are you insane?

32
00:01:10,660 --> 00:01:11,960
Uh...

33
00:01:12,160 --> 00:01:13,289
Grandpa has been quiet...

34
00:01:13,310 --> 00:01:15,110
He hasn't come into my dreams lately.

35
00:01:16,070 --> 00:01:17,030
Well...

36
00:01:17,030 --> 00:01:19,020
I have a lot of things I want to ask him.

37
00:01:19,020 --> 00:01:20,030
By the way...

38
00:01:20,039 --> 00:01:21,050
let me ask you.

39
00:01:24,620 --> 00:01:25,630
Take a look at this.

40
00:01:27,039 --> 00:01:28,940
Does Grandpa have
a lot of these photos?

41
00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:31,140
And did he go to Nakhon Sawan often?

42
00:01:31,950 --> 00:01:32,740
I can't see it.

43
00:01:32,740 --> 00:01:33,509
You can't?

44
00:01:33,509 --> 00:01:33,900
Here.

45
00:01:34,460 --> 00:01:35,160
Too close!

46
00:01:35,160 --> 00:01:36,539
Ugh...who can see from that distance?

47
00:01:36,590 --> 00:01:37,840
From wherever you can see it, then.

48
00:01:40,979 --> 00:01:41,990
Well...

49
00:01:42,120 --> 00:01:44,700
He visited Nakhon Sawan
every two or three months.

50
00:01:46,820 --> 00:01:49,500
Gramps probably missed you
and your mother a lot.

51
00:01:52,310 --> 00:01:54,080
But...there are more photos.

52
00:01:55,020 --> 00:01:56,360
I think they're kept in the safe.

53
00:01:56,360 --> 00:01:58,990
He keeps everything important in there.

54
00:01:59,720 --> 00:02:01,220
Wow...

55
00:02:01,510 --> 00:02:06,020
Did Grandpa miss
my mom that much?

56
00:02:06,150 --> 00:02:08,289
I already told you,

57
00:02:08,300 --> 00:02:10,570
I just want to see your mother's face.

58
00:02:11,410 --> 00:02:12,470
If she were not so stubborn

59
00:02:12,480 --> 00:02:15,060
and married the man I chose,
she would be better off by now.

60
00:02:15,230 --> 00:02:16,940
She would not have to fry rice

61
00:02:16,940 --> 00:02:18,740
to repay the bank loans.

62
00:02:19,420 --> 00:02:21,800
You're as stubborn as a mule too, Grandpa.

63
00:02:23,240 --> 00:02:24,280
Hey...

64
00:02:25,100 --> 00:02:26,100
did you talk to yourself?

65
00:02:26,130 --> 00:02:26,790
Are you insane?

66
00:02:26,829 --> 00:02:27,370
Huh?

67
00:02:28,060 --> 00:02:29,280
I was mumbling to the photo.

68
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:30,420
It reminds me of the past

69
00:02:30,420 --> 00:02:32,170
since I haven't seen
this photo in a long time...

70
00:02:32,340 --> 00:02:33,579
You're unhinged.

71
00:02:33,579 --> 00:02:34,420
I'm leaving.

72
00:02:34,420 --> 00:02:35,400
- Mm...
- You're weird.

73
00:02:35,770 --> 00:02:36,579
- Whoa!
- What...

74
00:02:37,710 --> 00:02:38,380
What's wrong? What?

75
00:02:38,380 --> 00:02:39,160
What are you?

76
00:02:39,160 --> 00:02:39,670
Huh?

77
00:02:39,960 --> 00:02:40,570
Ugh...

78
00:02:40,840 --> 00:02:41,840
Hey...

79
00:02:42,500 --> 00:02:43,390
I'm Dax.

80
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:44,660
This is Dax.

81
00:02:46,070 --> 00:02:46,790
Dax?

82
00:02:46,990 --> 00:02:48,300
Why are you dressed like that?

83
00:02:48,300 --> 00:02:49,350
Why didn't you get changed?

84
00:02:49,490 --> 00:02:50,390
Well, last night,

85
00:02:50,390 --> 00:02:51,820
we finished filming very late.

86
00:02:51,820 --> 00:02:53,050
- Today, I had an early call.
- Mm.

87
00:02:53,060 --> 00:02:54,530
- Tomorrow, too.
- Oh.

88
00:02:54,540 --> 00:02:55,820
So I decided to keep this on.

89
00:02:56,020 --> 00:02:57,030
I don't wanna change anymore.

90
00:02:57,370 --> 00:02:58,540
Whoa, the schedule is pretty tight.

91
00:02:58,710 --> 00:03:00,080
Can I sleep in your room tonight?

92
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:00,970
What?

93
00:03:01,280 --> 00:03:02,660
I already gave you a room
on the third floor, though.

94
00:03:02,660 --> 00:03:03,370
Why don't you sleep there?

95
00:03:03,370 --> 00:03:04,080
Ugh...

96
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:05,460
Who could fall asleep like that?

97
00:03:05,480 --> 00:03:07,430
The next room
is drinking and making a racket.

98
00:03:07,590 --> 00:03:08,320
Which room is it?

99
00:03:12,740 --> 00:03:13,400
Whoa!

100
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:13,870
Sheesh...

101
00:03:13,870 --> 00:03:14,670
Hear that?

102
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:16,490
They're this loud?

103
00:03:16,570 --> 00:03:17,770
Oh, they're very loud, huh?

104
00:03:23,010 --> 00:03:26,560
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

105
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:30,820
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

106
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:38,660
♫Every step we take has a meaning♫

107
00:03:40,030 --> 00:03:44,760
♫No path is ever meaningless♫

108
00:03:47,079 --> 00:03:53,320
♫As long as our hearts keep searching♫

109
00:03:54,260 --> 00:03:58,810
♫One day, we'll find
what we're yearning for♫

110
00:03:58,829 --> 00:04:02,410
♫Walking alone is fine,
but it's better when you're by my side♫

111
00:04:02,410 --> 00:04:06,000
♫It won't be lonely
when you're here to walk beside♫

112
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:09,560
♫Like a love that waits, waits at the D Dorm♫

113
00:04:09,570 --> 00:04:12,000
♫Like a love that remains,
remains at the dorm♫

114
00:04:12,020 --> 00:04:18,920
♫Meaningful love and good things
await on every path♫

115
00:04:18,950 --> 00:04:26,150
♫It might not be a coincidence
that we get to meet♫

116
00:04:26,150 --> 00:04:33,350
♫There might be hidden meanings
on the path beneath our feet♫

117
00:04:33,350 --> 00:04:40,470
♫Perhaps the D Dorm
is what led me to meet you♫

118
00:04:40,490 --> 00:04:44,360
[The D Dorm]

119
00:04:59,370 --> 00:05:01,140
Your solo sounds
like you're asking for trouble.

120
00:05:01,250 --> 00:05:03,120
Isn't that a bit too loud, dude?

121
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:06,720
[Dope, occupation: high school student]

122
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:08,600
What's there to be afraid of?

123
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:10,100
His father can handle this anyway.

124
00:05:10,210 --> 00:05:11,120
This way!

125
00:05:11,120 --> 00:05:11,750
Oh?

126
00:05:13,600 --> 00:05:16,360
[Dump, occupation: high school student]

127
00:05:16,590 --> 00:05:17,410
His father

128
00:05:17,430 --> 00:05:18,260
doesn't need yarn,

129
00:05:18,280 --> 00:05:19,320
thread,

130
00:05:19,390 --> 00:05:20,900
or rope!

131
00:05:23,420 --> 00:05:26,150
[Dape, occupation: high school student]

132
00:05:26,330 --> 00:05:29,040
Cause my father can pull the strings!

133
00:05:29,180 --> 00:05:30,720
If anyone in this dorm has an issue with us,

134
00:05:30,730 --> 00:05:32,620
just say my father's name.

135
00:05:33,690 --> 00:05:34,920
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

136
00:05:36,040 --> 00:05:36,880
Surachet!

137
00:05:38,070 --> 00:05:39,070
Surachet!

138
00:05:40,170 --> 00:05:41,100
Surachet!

139
00:05:42,140 --> 00:05:43,020
Surachet!

140
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:44,470
Ugh!

141
00:05:45,290 --> 00:05:46,010
Use it to threaten them,

142
00:05:46,010 --> 00:05:47,180
not to mock me!

143
00:05:51,060 --> 00:05:51,610
Hey.

144
00:05:57,220 --> 00:05:58,170
- Louder.
- Do it louder.

145
00:05:59,880 --> 00:06:00,680
Call out to him.

146
00:06:00,680 --> 00:06:02,150
Hey!

147
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:04,210
Ugh...

148
00:06:04,210 --> 00:06:05,560
Stop making loud noises.

149
00:06:05,560 --> 00:06:07,320
It's disturbing other tenants!

150
00:06:07,930 --> 00:06:09,620
Who told you about us?

151
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:11,090
I did.

152
00:06:11,090 --> 00:06:12,040
- Wait.
- Whoa.

153
00:06:13,340 --> 00:06:16,380
Am I so drunk that
I'm seeing a bald softshell turtle?!

154
00:06:16,380 --> 00:06:17,320
Wow...

155
00:06:17,320 --> 00:06:18,210
I'm a kappa.

156
00:06:18,950 --> 00:06:19,560
Kappa...

157
00:06:19,560 --> 00:06:22,550
We were just celebrating after our exams.

158
00:06:22,710 --> 00:06:23,900
Hey,

159
00:06:24,350 --> 00:06:26,370
I understand you want to celebrate
after your exams,

160
00:06:26,370 --> 00:06:27,620
but be more considerate.

161
00:06:27,660 --> 00:06:29,100
You're disturbing the others.

162
00:06:29,100 --> 00:06:29,750
Yeah.

163
00:06:29,750 --> 00:06:31,340
That's all I ask.

164
00:06:31,980 --> 00:06:33,270
If you asked...

165
00:06:34,040 --> 00:06:34,870
then I'll humor you!

166
00:06:36,020 --> 00:06:37,180
Without further ado,

167
00:06:37,180 --> 00:06:39,250
please enjoy the performance by

168
00:06:39,250 --> 00:06:41,450
Wat Nong Tao Ngoi School!

169
00:06:42,760 --> 00:06:43,659
Ugh, you...

170
00:06:43,659 --> 00:06:44,700
Every time you see a mic,

171
00:06:44,700 --> 00:06:45,560
you have to be an MC, huh?

172
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:46,200
- Yeah.
- What?

173
00:06:46,200 --> 00:06:47,120
It's muscle memory.

174
00:06:47,120 --> 00:06:47,730
Mm, understandable.

175
00:06:47,790 --> 00:06:48,450
Ugh...

176
00:06:48,770 --> 00:06:49,620
Guys,

177
00:06:49,620 --> 00:06:51,280
this is your first warning.

178
00:06:51,290 --> 00:06:52,850
Don't let there be a second time.

179
00:06:52,850 --> 00:06:53,980
What if there's a second time?

180
00:06:54,840 --> 00:06:55,840
There shouldn't be a third time.

181
00:06:55,840 --> 00:06:56,720
What about a fourth time?

182
00:06:56,720 --> 00:06:57,940
Don't let it happen a fourth time.

183
00:06:57,940 --> 00:06:58,800
Ugh!

184
00:06:58,980 --> 00:06:59,480
Hey,

185
00:06:59,480 --> 00:07:01,110
have you been beaten up
by a kappa before?

186
00:07:02,180 --> 00:07:03,010
Kappa?

187
00:07:03,390 --> 00:07:05,320
- You want some?!
- Whoa, whoa, whoa.

188
00:07:06,050 --> 00:07:06,950
Whoa, kiddos!

189
00:07:06,950 --> 00:07:09,060
Just high schoolers, yet so cocky.

190
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:11,000
Why don't you tell your parents
to come talk to me, hm?

191
00:07:11,010 --> 00:07:11,450
Yeah.

192
00:07:11,750 --> 00:07:12,990
Well, if my father came,

193
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:15,390
will you be able to carry
the consequences?

194
00:07:15,810 --> 00:07:16,960
Why would I need to carry anything?!

195
00:07:17,130 --> 00:07:18,810
Is your father diabetic
and can't walk on his own?

196
00:07:18,810 --> 00:07:20,190
- Hey...
- Whoa...

197
00:07:20,190 --> 00:07:21,640
Insulting my friend's father like this...

198
00:07:21,690 --> 00:07:23,280
- You want some?!
- Whoa, whoa.

199
00:07:23,290 --> 00:07:24,480
- Chill.
- He's fierce.

200
00:07:24,480 --> 00:07:26,520
He jumps headfirst into things, huh?

201
00:07:26,530 --> 00:07:28,390
Acting as if you were corn aphids.

202
00:07:28,390 --> 00:07:30,240
Since you came all the way here,

203
00:07:30,580 --> 00:07:32,840
let us sing you a cute song.

204
00:07:34,190 --> 00:07:35,790
Three, two, one...

205
00:07:35,810 --> 00:07:37,840
- ♫Goose kiss,♫
- ♫Starfish kiss,♫

206
00:07:37,880 --> 00:07:38,890
♫Goldfish kiss,♫

207
00:07:38,920 --> 00:07:39,980
♫Rooster kiss,♫

208
00:07:39,980 --> 00:07:42,990
♫Any kisses only for you♫

209
00:07:43,140 --> 00:07:43,680
Go.

210
00:07:43,680 --> 00:07:45,810
♫Kiss, kiss, kiss, kiss, kiss♫

211
00:07:45,810 --> 00:07:46,900
♫This kiss is for you♫

212
00:07:46,900 --> 00:07:47,340
Yeah.

213
00:07:47,340 --> 00:07:49,380
♫Kiss, kiss, kiss, kiss, kiss♫

214
00:07:49,380 --> 00:07:50,830
♫This heart is for you♫

215
00:07:50,830 --> 00:07:52,700
♫My heart, my heart, all for you♫

216
00:07:52,700 --> 00:07:54,020
♫This love is for no one else but you♫

217
00:07:54,020 --> 00:07:54,820
- Ugh!
- ♫Kiss♫

218
00:07:54,820 --> 00:07:55,940
Go kiss your dad, then!

219
00:07:55,940 --> 00:07:56,400
Huh?!

220
00:07:57,200 --> 00:07:58,620
You should stop them!

221
00:07:58,820 --> 00:07:59,790
Why didn't you stop them?

222
00:07:59,790 --> 00:08:00,990
♫Kiss, kiss, kiss♫

223
00:08:00,990 --> 00:08:02,190
♫This kiss is for you♫

224
00:08:02,190 --> 00:08:04,100
♫Rooster kiss, starfish kiss,♫

225
00:08:04,100 --> 00:08:05,790
♫Goose kiss, kitty kiss,♫

226
00:08:05,820 --> 00:08:07,700
- Peek-a-boo...
- Boo...

227
00:08:08,680 --> 00:08:09,400
Ugh!

228
00:08:10,080 --> 00:08:11,250
Hey...

229
00:08:11,250 --> 00:08:13,440
I think I'm fine with them

230
00:08:13,450 --> 00:08:15,040
singing this cute song

231
00:08:15,170 --> 00:08:16,280
from such a great agency.

232
00:08:16,590 --> 00:08:17,770
Mm, that's true...

233
00:08:17,940 --> 00:08:18,920
He's right.

234
00:08:19,330 --> 00:08:20,790
If you sing this song, it's fine.

235
00:08:20,820 --> 00:08:21,830
Mm.

236
00:08:21,860 --> 00:08:23,180
Just keep it down, alright?

237
00:08:23,440 --> 00:08:25,040
So, we can sing this song, right?

238
00:08:25,290 --> 00:08:26,190
Mm, I'm okay with that.

239
00:08:26,620 --> 00:08:27,160
Go.

240
00:08:27,160 --> 00:08:28,710
Alright, let's go.

241
00:08:28,920 --> 00:08:30,990
We'll keep it down, then.

242
00:08:30,990 --> 00:08:31,640
Mm.

243
00:08:39,450 --> 00:08:41,799
Are we really gonna
play only cute songs, dude?

244
00:08:41,919 --> 00:08:43,090
Yeah, it's...

245
00:08:43,100 --> 00:08:45,250
We've become softies. We're so over.

246
00:08:50,620 --> 00:08:51,720
You got a plan?

247
00:08:54,080 --> 00:08:56,760
[The D Dorm]

248
00:08:58,170 --> 00:08:58,960
Mm...

249
00:08:59,280 --> 00:09:00,950
Mmm... Ooh...

250
00:09:03,350 --> 00:09:05,750
Mmm... Ooh...

251
00:09:10,550 --> 00:09:12,130
Mm...

252
00:09:14,070 --> 00:09:16,010
Gaysorn...

253
00:09:16,340 --> 00:09:17,800
I miss you.

254
00:09:19,130 --> 00:09:20,040
Ugh, Grandpa!

255
00:09:20,580 --> 00:09:21,660
What are you doing?!

256
00:09:21,660 --> 00:09:22,380
Disgusting!!

257
00:09:22,880 --> 00:09:23,750
What do you mean?

258
00:09:23,970 --> 00:09:24,360
Huh?

259
00:09:24,680 --> 00:09:25,540
What is disgusting?

260
00:09:25,540 --> 00:09:26,090
What?

261
00:09:26,370 --> 00:09:26,930
You were eating noodles?

262
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:27,850
What?

263
00:09:28,010 --> 00:09:28,920
Why did you have to make that noise?

264
00:09:28,920 --> 00:09:30,350
Well, it is spicy!

265
00:09:30,690 --> 00:09:31,550
I don't mind the noise...

266
00:09:31,550 --> 00:09:32,560
but why did you move
your hand like that?

267
00:09:32,600 --> 00:09:34,720
I am mixing the chili into the noodles.

268
00:09:34,840 --> 00:09:36,460
Why were you moaning
Grandma Gaysorn's name?

269
00:09:36,460 --> 00:09:37,750
Well, this shop...

270
00:09:37,750 --> 00:09:38,890
has been open for a long time.

271
00:09:38,900 --> 00:09:40,690
I used to eat here with Gaysorn,

272
00:09:40,690 --> 00:09:42,940
so eating this again reminds me of her.

273
00:09:42,940 --> 00:09:44,150
Ugh...

274
00:09:44,850 --> 00:09:45,950
Can you eat quietly?

275
00:09:45,970 --> 00:09:48,180
Don't sit there calling
Grandma Gaysorn's name like that.

276
00:09:50,150 --> 00:09:50,680
Hey.

277
00:09:50,970 --> 00:09:52,070
- Mmm...
- Whoa.

278
00:09:52,070 --> 00:09:52,890
Ooh...

279
00:09:52,890 --> 00:09:54,400
Stop making that noise.

280
00:09:54,550 --> 00:09:55,740
Eat quietly, Grandpa.

281
00:09:56,370 --> 00:09:57,060
Wait.

282
00:09:57,350 --> 00:09:58,040
Why...

283
00:09:58,230 --> 00:09:59,430
is there so much food?

284
00:09:59,430 --> 00:10:00,290
Don't tell me...

285
00:10:00,410 --> 00:10:01,560
you stole from a three-way crossroads?

286
00:10:02,740 --> 00:10:03,350
Hey,

287
00:10:03,650 --> 00:10:05,570
I am not a wandering spirit.

288
00:10:05,570 --> 00:10:06,950
I have a place to dwell!

289
00:10:06,950 --> 00:10:07,830
Well, you seem like one.

290
00:10:08,910 --> 00:10:10,440
I do not know either.

291
00:10:10,440 --> 00:10:12,250
Perhaps someone gave me
their offerings.

292
00:10:12,680 --> 00:10:13,410
Who, though?

293
00:10:13,780 --> 00:10:14,520
Danis?

294
00:10:14,520 --> 00:10:15,520
I do not think so.

295
00:10:16,050 --> 00:10:16,700
Mom?

296
00:10:16,970 --> 00:10:18,240
Mm...maybe?

297
00:10:18,240 --> 00:10:19,060
I don't think so,

298
00:10:19,060 --> 00:10:19,820
she hates your guts.

299
00:10:20,290 --> 00:10:20,810
Wait...

300
00:10:20,980 --> 00:10:21,570
maybe it was me.

301
00:10:21,570 --> 00:10:23,100
Oh, thank you so much,
my beloved grandson.

302
00:10:23,110 --> 00:10:24,610
It's such a waste of my time, though.

303
00:10:24,620 --> 00:10:25,640
Wow, you ungrateful grandson.

304
00:10:26,640 --> 00:10:27,660
Who is it, then, Grandpa?

305
00:10:28,990 --> 00:10:30,020
Where did Thai music come from?

306
00:10:30,970 --> 00:10:31,610
Hey,

307
00:10:31,860 --> 00:10:32,640
do you hear that?

308
00:10:32,640 --> 00:10:34,050
Who is playing ranat in the morning?

309
00:10:35,130 --> 00:10:35,720
Hey...

310
00:10:36,360 --> 00:10:36,950
Wait.

311
00:10:37,700 --> 00:10:38,660
- Whoa...
- It's loud.

312
00:10:38,660 --> 00:10:39,700
What is happening?

313
00:10:40,330 --> 00:10:41,440
- Huh?
- Grandpa?

314
00:10:41,570 --> 00:10:42,170
What's wrong?

315
00:10:42,360 --> 00:10:42,950
I do not know...

316
00:10:42,990 --> 00:10:43,440
Whoa!

317
00:10:43,440 --> 00:10:43,930
Hey!

318
00:10:44,470 --> 00:10:45,160
Grandpa?

319
00:10:45,350 --> 00:10:46,210
What's wrong?

320
00:10:46,860 --> 00:10:48,300
I do not know either!

321
00:10:50,320 --> 00:10:52,120
- Dobby, help me!
- Whoa!

322
00:10:52,250 --> 00:10:53,750
Dobby, help me!

323
00:10:53,750 --> 00:10:56,700
- Dobby!
- Grandpa!

324
00:10:57,110 --> 00:10:58,120
Grandpa!

325
00:10:58,210 --> 00:10:58,690
Oh, crap!

326
00:10:58,690 --> 00:10:59,830
What happened, Grandpa?!

327
00:11:12,010 --> 00:11:12,840
What even is this?

328
00:11:13,800 --> 00:11:16,320
Dobby, please help me.

329
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:18,370
I do not want to watch this ritual dance.

330
00:11:18,370 --> 00:11:20,090
I was forced to be here!

331
00:11:22,720 --> 00:11:23,380
Hey...

332
00:11:23,380 --> 00:11:24,010
Hm?

333
00:11:24,010 --> 00:11:25,930
Why is Auntie Duang suddenly
dancing here?

334
00:11:25,930 --> 00:11:27,710
What's with all these offerings?

335
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:29,750
Auntie Duang had a dream

336
00:11:29,750 --> 00:11:31,050
that Gramps came
to tell her lottery numbers.

337
00:11:31,290 --> 00:11:33,350
The tenants bought it, and many won.

338
00:11:33,350 --> 00:11:35,440
That's why they all came to worship Gramps.

339
00:11:36,520 --> 00:11:38,820
I have never told anyone anything.

340
00:11:38,820 --> 00:11:40,380
They came up with that on their own!

341
00:11:40,380 --> 00:11:42,760
You know I do not know
how to get into people's dreams.

342
00:11:43,370 --> 00:11:44,150
Yeah...

343
00:11:44,280 --> 00:11:44,940
- Daeng.
- Hm?

344
00:11:44,960 --> 00:11:45,810
Look at Auntie Duang.

345
00:11:46,040 --> 00:11:47,830
She met Gramps,
and he gave her the numbers.

346
00:11:48,010 --> 00:11:49,060
What about you?

347
00:11:49,320 --> 00:11:51,250
Why didn't you and Dawin get anything?

348
00:11:51,250 --> 00:11:52,140
You're no good.

349
00:11:52,380 --> 00:11:52,930
Hm?

350
00:11:53,100 --> 00:11:53,750
Hey...

351
00:11:54,240 --> 00:11:55,180
Sadhu, Gramps,

352
00:11:55,490 --> 00:11:57,140
if you let me win the lottery,

353
00:11:57,170 --> 00:11:58,360
I won't keep a single baht.

354
00:11:58,360 --> 00:11:59,400
I'll give it all to the tenants.

355
00:11:59,400 --> 00:12:00,750
- Not you too...
- Won't you regret that?

356
00:12:00,800 --> 00:12:01,860
Why would I?
It's not gonna happen anyway.

357
00:12:01,860 --> 00:12:02,340
What?

358
00:12:02,340 --> 00:12:03,350
Oh, not you too.

359
00:12:03,480 --> 00:12:04,100
Gramps,

360
00:12:04,100 --> 00:12:05,070
to keep it simple, for this draw,

361
00:12:05,070 --> 00:12:06,750
give me three of those.

362
00:12:06,950 --> 00:12:07,700
Puppies?

363
00:12:07,720 --> 00:12:08,360
Nails.

364
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:09,860
We've been together for so long,

365
00:12:09,870 --> 00:12:10,960
yet our jokes never clicked.

366
00:12:10,960 --> 00:12:12,080
I don't want the numbers anymore.

367
00:12:12,080 --> 00:12:13,280
Go break his neck instead.

368
00:12:13,280 --> 00:12:13,800
Hey!

369
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:14,510
I'll break your neck.

370
00:12:14,510 --> 00:12:15,400
I'm older than you!

371
00:12:15,570 --> 00:12:16,010
Don't...

372
00:12:16,550 --> 00:12:17,330
Gramps...

373
00:12:17,750 --> 00:12:19,540
- Ugh...
- They fight, as expected.

374
00:12:21,200 --> 00:12:24,040
I danced just like you asked, Gramps.

375
00:12:24,780 --> 00:12:28,210
If you give me
a big win in this lottery draw,

376
00:12:28,210 --> 00:12:29,680
I'll put on a big show for you.

377
00:12:29,750 --> 00:12:32,150
Whether it's Thai traditional dance,

378
00:12:32,500 --> 00:12:35,220
Chinese traditional dance,

379
00:12:35,360 --> 00:12:36,270
or...

380
00:12:37,290 --> 00:12:38,360
Indonesian traditional dance,

381
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:41,750
or even

382
00:12:42,010 --> 00:12:43,380
twerking!

383
00:12:43,380 --> 00:12:44,480
Twerking!

384
00:12:44,480 --> 00:12:45,620
Twerking!

385
00:12:45,620 --> 00:12:46,440
So annoying!!

386
00:12:46,440 --> 00:12:47,940
I'm gonna give you the full show!

387
00:12:47,940 --> 00:12:48,810
No need!

388
00:12:48,810 --> 00:12:50,400
I do not want any of that!

389
00:12:53,900 --> 00:12:54,560
Gramps,

390
00:12:54,770 --> 00:12:55,430
how about this?

391
00:12:55,430 --> 00:12:56,470
If I won the first prize in the lottery...

392
00:12:56,470 --> 00:12:57,770
Forget this little show.

393
00:12:57,770 --> 00:12:59,150
I'd hire Rabiab Wathasilp

394
00:12:59,160 --> 00:13:00,410
for seven days and seven nights.

395
00:13:00,950 --> 00:13:01,580
Ugh...

396
00:13:01,580 --> 00:13:03,280
Guard Dum, please don't go that far.

397
00:13:03,350 --> 00:13:04,740
The tenants have already complained

398
00:13:04,850 --> 00:13:07,360
about these offerings.

399
00:13:07,520 --> 00:13:09,490
And there are also those kids
in Room 310.

400
00:13:09,490 --> 00:13:11,010
- Yeah.
- God...they're loud.

401
00:13:11,020 --> 00:13:12,600
I'm getting a lot of complaints.

402
00:13:12,920 --> 00:13:14,880
Come on, Danis,

403
00:13:14,880 --> 00:13:16,550
I'm only asking for a small space.

404
00:13:16,550 --> 00:13:17,590
I promise

405
00:13:17,600 --> 00:13:19,260
I won't cause any trouble,

406
00:13:19,260 --> 00:13:20,770
unlike those kids in Room 310.

407
00:13:21,480 --> 00:13:24,440
Prime Minister Noo gave us 60/40.

408
00:13:24,810 --> 00:13:26,900
But Gramps can give us
a hundred times more here.

409
00:13:26,900 --> 00:13:28,550
I guarantee the economy will prosper!

410
00:13:28,550 --> 00:13:29,360
Ugh...

411
00:13:29,360 --> 00:13:30,250
That is even worse.

412
00:13:30,250 --> 00:13:31,640
- What economy, Auntie?
- Right?

413
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:32,970
You'll know soon enough.

414
00:13:33,490 --> 00:13:34,420
Oh, that doesn't sound good.

415
00:13:36,130 --> 00:13:37,680
Sadhu, sadhu.

416
00:13:39,320 --> 00:13:41,470
[The D Dorm]

417
00:13:41,640 --> 00:13:42,410
Come this way.
[Gramps' Vow Offerings]

418
00:13:42,410 --> 00:13:43,660
One hundred and ninety-nine times two.

419
00:13:43,660 --> 00:13:44,430
Your change.

420
00:13:44,430 --> 00:13:45,620
Thanks...

421
00:13:45,860 --> 00:13:47,640
Sadhu, sadhu.

422
00:13:48,210 --> 00:13:49,790
Wow...

423
00:13:49,850 --> 00:13:52,330
This is only going to make
your economy prosper, isn't it?

424
00:13:53,620 --> 00:13:56,050
Well, have some empathy for me.

425
00:13:56,070 --> 00:13:57,860
I'm a single mom with two kids,

426
00:13:57,880 --> 00:13:59,180
and I'm getting old.

427
00:13:59,180 --> 00:14:01,610
My boys are still growing up, too.

428
00:14:04,800 --> 00:14:05,300
Mm...

429
00:14:07,400 --> 00:14:08,600
- Oh...
- Oh, wow...

430
00:14:08,680 --> 00:14:09,780
Whoa...

431
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:12,370
- Hey.
- Ooh...

432
00:14:12,910 --> 00:14:13,900
What are you doing?

433
00:14:14,410 --> 00:14:14,900
Huh?

434
00:14:15,350 --> 00:14:17,130
I want to drink bubble tea,
but I feel guilty,

435
00:14:17,400 --> 00:14:18,360
so I do it while working out.

436
00:14:18,640 --> 00:14:19,410
See?

437
00:14:19,410 --> 00:14:20,520
A real gym rat spotted...

438
00:14:22,280 --> 00:14:22,780
By the way, Mom?

439
00:14:22,780 --> 00:14:23,280
Hm?

440
00:14:23,280 --> 00:14:24,950
Have you talked to Danis

441
00:14:25,170 --> 00:14:26,530
about building a shrine for Gramps?

442
00:14:26,530 --> 00:14:27,560
- Hm?
- Huh?

443
00:14:27,760 --> 00:14:28,570
What shrine?

444
00:14:32,920 --> 00:14:34,820
I was just planning ahead

445
00:14:34,900 --> 00:14:37,350
in case Gramps becomes popular.

446
00:14:37,350 --> 00:14:39,350
We can build a shrine to get
lots of people to come worship him.

447
00:14:39,350 --> 00:14:41,170
People will rent rooms in the dorm,

448
00:14:41,170 --> 00:14:43,200
and my business will boom.

449
00:14:43,200 --> 00:14:44,470
Then everyone

450
00:14:44,470 --> 00:14:45,750
will be complaining,

451
00:14:45,770 --> 00:14:47,230
"I'm so rich, I can't take it anymore!"

452
00:14:47,250 --> 00:14:48,420
Whoa...

453
00:14:48,420 --> 00:14:50,050
I can't, I can't, I can't...

454
00:14:50,980 --> 00:14:52,550
I can't see that working out, Auntie.

455
00:14:53,420 --> 00:14:55,760
If people know this dorm is haunted,
who's gonna purchase it?

456
00:14:56,020 --> 00:14:56,610
Purchase?

457
00:14:58,550 --> 00:14:59,200
Purchase what?

458
00:14:59,630 --> 00:15:01,560
Didn't you say you weren't
going to sell this dorm anymore?

459
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:10,160
You misheard me.

460
00:15:10,550 --> 00:15:11,920
I... I mean "hire purchase."

461
00:15:12,520 --> 00:15:13,460
Think about it.

462
00:15:13,460 --> 00:15:15,010
If people know this dorm is haunted,

463
00:15:15,350 --> 00:15:16,610
will they want to live here?

464
00:15:16,660 --> 00:15:18,010
No one would dare rent a room here.

465
00:15:18,160 --> 00:15:20,510
Not everyone's crazy about
the lottery like you, Auntie.

466
00:15:24,660 --> 00:15:26,620
Please don't go that far, Auntie.

467
00:15:26,620 --> 00:15:28,570
It'll disturb the other tenants.

468
00:15:29,090 --> 00:15:29,750
That's right, Auntie.

469
00:15:30,410 --> 00:15:30,950
Right?

470
00:15:31,780 --> 00:15:32,360
Yeah...

471
00:15:33,350 --> 00:15:33,920
Oh!

472
00:15:42,120 --> 00:15:43,060
Stay still.

473
00:15:46,680 --> 00:15:47,540
Hold on to this, Dum.

474
00:15:47,570 --> 00:15:48,150
Okay.

475
00:15:48,170 --> 00:15:49,040
Uh, Mr. Drip?

476
00:15:49,490 --> 00:15:50,360
Can you please grab...

477
00:15:50,370 --> 00:15:51,510
that screwdriver for me?

478
00:15:51,520 --> 00:15:52,580
Of course, Handyman.

479
00:15:53,090 --> 00:15:54,220
♫Wh...who said I'm shivering?♫

480
00:15:54,220 --> 00:15:54,950
Oh, crap!

481
00:15:55,740 --> 00:15:56,440
[DO-MUN-DRIP]

482
00:15:56,450 --> 00:15:57,170
Whoa...

483
00:15:59,050 --> 00:16:00,360
How captivating!

484
00:16:00,740 --> 00:16:02,150
This is art.

485
00:16:31,760 --> 00:16:32,440
What even is that?

486
00:16:35,970 --> 00:16:37,000
Can I hold your hand?

487
00:16:37,040 --> 00:16:38,230
- Ugh!
- Let me hold your hand.

488
00:16:38,290 --> 00:16:38,860
Let go!

489
00:16:38,880 --> 00:16:40,080
Don't touch me! Let go!

490
00:16:40,260 --> 00:16:40,900
What are you doing?

491
00:16:41,140 --> 00:16:41,750
I see...

492
00:16:41,750 --> 00:16:43,250
Double double this this,

493
00:16:43,250 --> 00:16:44,760
double double that that,

494
00:16:44,760 --> 00:16:46,140
double this, double that,

495
00:16:46,140 --> 00:16:47,580
double double this that.

496
00:16:47,580 --> 00:16:48,350
- Hey!
- Ugh!

497
00:16:50,210 --> 00:16:51,120
Hey...

498
00:16:51,270 --> 00:16:53,120
you're still trying to hold
Daeng the Handyman's hand, Dawin?

499
00:16:54,380 --> 00:16:56,150
I don't think holding hands

500
00:16:56,350 --> 00:16:58,440
has anything to do with you seeing
Gramps' ghost the other day.

501
00:16:58,550 --> 00:16:59,690
It doesn't.

502
00:16:59,960 --> 00:17:02,200
My brother and I have been
holding hands since we were kids,

503
00:17:02,330 --> 00:17:03,720
but I've never seen a ghost before.

504
00:17:03,720 --> 00:17:04,819
Look.

505
00:17:06,950 --> 00:17:07,859
What...?

506
00:17:08,880 --> 00:17:09,630
Can you see ghosts, Guard Dum?

507
00:17:10,089 --> 00:17:10,730
I'm getting electrocuted...

508
00:17:10,730 --> 00:17:11,349
- Whoa?
- Let go.

509
00:17:11,569 --> 00:17:12,599
I'll kick you off!

510
00:17:12,619 --> 00:17:13,480
Daeng... You...

511
00:17:13,640 --> 00:17:14,970
Ugh, I can't let go of this either.

512
00:17:18,140 --> 00:17:18,960
Ugh!

513
00:17:24,630 --> 00:17:25,859
I was wondering...

514
00:17:25,940 --> 00:17:27,869
If we held hands,

515
00:17:28,260 --> 00:17:29,220
would we see any ghosts?

516
00:17:35,730 --> 00:17:37,400
I don't see any "ghosts"

517
00:17:38,820 --> 00:17:40,100
Only a "good" eye candy

518
00:17:41,040 --> 00:17:41,620
Huh?

519
00:17:43,140 --> 00:17:43,620
Uh...

520
00:17:44,150 --> 00:17:45,210
Oops... I'm sorry.

521
00:17:45,610 --> 00:17:46,210
Um...

522
00:17:46,840 --> 00:17:47,750
Dawin!

523
00:17:47,750 --> 00:17:49,270
Why would you want to see
Gramps' ghost again?

524
00:17:49,470 --> 00:17:51,360
Do you want to ask for
lottery numbers...like Mom did?

525
00:17:53,010 --> 00:17:53,750
Well...

526
00:17:54,340 --> 00:17:56,180
I just want to prove

527
00:17:56,580 --> 00:17:58,120
if I have the ability to see ghosts.

528
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:02,090
If you want to see ghosts,

529
00:18:02,100 --> 00:18:04,420
there are many other ways
apart from holding my brother's hand.

530
00:18:04,730 --> 00:18:05,560
To keep it simple,

531
00:18:05,560 --> 00:18:06,880
you can look between your legs.

532
00:18:07,940 --> 00:18:09,000
- Ow!
- Ow...

533
00:18:09,020 --> 00:18:09,540
Whoa...

534
00:18:09,540 --> 00:18:11,750
Come on, Daeng...

535
00:18:12,170 --> 00:18:13,700
I tried a lot of methods

536
00:18:14,050 --> 00:18:15,060
ever since I was little,

537
00:18:15,220 --> 00:18:16,370
but nothing worked.

538
00:18:16,750 --> 00:18:17,750
What?

539
00:18:18,060 --> 00:18:18,950
Have you always...

540
00:18:18,950 --> 00:18:21,060
wanted to see ghosts ever since
you were young?

541
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:22,120
Why?

542
00:18:24,120 --> 00:18:25,440
I just want to see them.

543
00:18:25,650 --> 00:18:26,980
Why are you asking so many questions?

544
00:18:28,880 --> 00:18:30,120
I tried everything.

545
00:18:30,580 --> 00:18:31,840
From looking between my legs,

546
00:18:32,610 --> 00:18:33,730
wearing dead people's clothes,

547
00:18:34,570 --> 00:18:36,180
and I even applied the dirt from
seven cemeteries to my eyes.

548
00:18:37,060 --> 00:18:37,850
Oh.

549
00:18:38,340 --> 00:18:40,000
But there's one method I haven't tried yet.

550
00:18:40,140 --> 00:18:41,250
That is using a black dog's tear.

551
00:18:42,710 --> 00:18:43,210
What?

552
00:18:43,690 --> 00:18:44,860
Why didn't you try it?

553
00:18:45,020 --> 00:18:47,120
I don't know how to
make a dog cry.

554
00:18:47,600 --> 00:18:48,750
I've hit a dog with a stick before,

555
00:18:49,200 --> 00:18:50,450
but it bit me...

556
00:18:50,770 --> 00:18:52,340
So I ended up crying instead...

557
00:18:52,620 --> 00:18:53,750
- Whoa.
- Ugh...

558
00:18:54,080 --> 00:18:55,090
Serves you right!

559
00:18:55,090 --> 00:18:56,330
You were asking for trouble

560
00:18:56,330 --> 00:18:57,260
trying to see ghosts like that.

561
00:18:59,430 --> 00:19:00,470
Would you like to try it out tonight?

562
00:19:01,530 --> 00:19:02,360
If you want to,

563
00:19:02,370 --> 00:19:04,350
I'll take you to get a black dog's tear.

564
00:19:06,920 --> 00:19:07,930
I want to go, too, Guard!

565
00:19:08,560 --> 00:19:09,570
I've never seen

566
00:19:09,890 --> 00:19:11,380
a ghost before in my life.

567
00:19:11,600 --> 00:19:13,310
You're talking about ghosts here, not Justin Bieber.

568
00:19:13,570 --> 00:19:14,860
Why would you want to see ghosts anyway?

569
00:19:15,020 --> 00:19:16,200
You all can go if you want,

570
00:19:16,350 --> 00:19:17,360
but leave me out of this.

571
00:19:17,780 --> 00:19:18,950
Then...

572
00:19:18,960 --> 00:19:20,130
who would like to join me tonight?

573
00:19:20,140 --> 00:19:20,710
- Hey!
- Me!

574
00:19:21,440 --> 00:19:22,140
Ah...

575
00:19:22,140 --> 00:19:23,210
Everyone wants to go.

576
00:19:23,420 --> 00:19:24,370
You'll have to be alone tonight.

577
00:19:25,820 --> 00:19:26,830
- I'll go, too.
- Huh?

578
00:19:28,280 --> 00:19:30,350
[The D Dorm]

579
00:19:39,170 --> 00:19:42,790
Since when did my room become
a house of a softshell turtle?

580
00:19:44,860 --> 00:19:45,810
Grandpa, I feel bad for him.

581
00:19:45,820 --> 00:19:46,610
Let him rest.

582
00:19:47,590 --> 00:19:49,240
He was filming a series
late into the night,

583
00:19:49,390 --> 00:19:51,300
and he had to wake up
to the set again in the morning.

584
00:19:52,390 --> 00:19:53,400
Just let him get some sleep.

585
00:19:55,200 --> 00:19:56,150
Back then,

586
00:19:56,930 --> 00:19:57,930
your mother...

587
00:19:58,550 --> 00:20:00,950
asked me if she could have a pet turtle.

588
00:20:01,860 --> 00:20:03,350
But I did not allow her that,

589
00:20:04,550 --> 00:20:06,920
because turtle cages stink.

590
00:20:07,910 --> 00:20:08,920
Then your mother...

591
00:20:09,610 --> 00:20:10,980
tried to act cute

592
00:20:11,900 --> 00:20:12,910
by singing:

593
00:20:13,390 --> 00:20:15,730
♫Turtles have four legs♫

594
00:20:15,750 --> 00:20:18,200
♫Four feet marching our way♫

595
00:20:18,200 --> 00:20:20,810
♫Showing and hiding its head♫

596
00:20:22,530 --> 00:20:23,460
When she was little...

597
00:20:24,120 --> 00:20:25,330
she was adorable.

598
00:20:26,520 --> 00:20:27,920
But once she grew up...

599
00:20:28,960 --> 00:20:29,460
So stubborn.

600
00:20:30,400 --> 00:20:32,120
I wanted to shove ashes into her mouth.

601
00:20:33,150 --> 00:20:34,860
Well, Grandpa,

602
00:20:34,880 --> 00:20:36,190
if I were Mom,

603
00:20:36,760 --> 00:20:37,690
I'd chew those ashes.

604
00:20:37,690 --> 00:20:39,040
Chew, chew, chew, chew...

605
00:20:39,040 --> 00:20:40,330
And spit them right in your face.

606
00:20:41,960 --> 00:20:42,720
Hey, Grandpa,

607
00:20:42,720 --> 00:20:43,890
just admit it already that

608
00:20:43,900 --> 00:20:45,970
these days, my mom lives a happy life.

609
00:20:46,030 --> 00:20:47,220
She owns a house

610
00:20:47,510 --> 00:20:48,560
and a restaurant.

611
00:20:49,140 --> 00:20:50,730
She has a great husband.

612
00:20:51,040 --> 00:20:52,180
And most importantly,

613
00:20:53,310 --> 00:20:54,250
she has a son who is...

614
00:20:54,270 --> 00:20:55,190
so freaking handsome.

615
00:20:55,930 --> 00:20:57,440
"So freaking irritating" is more accurate.

616
00:20:58,550 --> 00:20:59,660
Back then...

617
00:21:00,020 --> 00:21:01,950
- What?
- If your mother had listened to me

618
00:21:01,950 --> 00:21:04,100
and married the person
I chose for her...

619
00:21:04,100 --> 00:21:05,190
Yeah? What would happen?

620
00:21:05,190 --> 00:21:06,780
Her life

621
00:21:07,120 --> 00:21:09,480
might have been better than this.

622
00:21:09,660 --> 00:21:11,670
She would not be drowning in debts.

623
00:21:11,750 --> 00:21:14,000
She would have had a rich

624
00:21:14,070 --> 00:21:15,750
and nice husband

625
00:21:16,010 --> 00:21:19,580
who provides for his family
and makes them happy.

626
00:21:21,070 --> 00:21:23,140
And when her kid grew up...

627
00:21:23,230 --> 00:21:24,440
they would've been a sweet child,

628
00:21:25,280 --> 00:21:26,800
not an irritating one like you are.

629
00:21:28,080 --> 00:21:28,760
Hey,

630
00:21:28,760 --> 00:21:30,400
it's passed down through our genes, alright?

631
00:21:30,760 --> 00:21:32,400
I'm irritating just like you are, Grandpa.

632
00:21:33,730 --> 00:21:34,550
Are you insulting me?!

633
00:21:35,750 --> 00:21:36,950
Well, there are only the two of us here.

634
00:21:36,950 --> 00:21:37,680
Who else would I be insulting?

635
00:21:37,690 --> 00:21:39,560
I thought you were insulting
that softshell turtle.

636
00:21:39,930 --> 00:21:40,890
Whoa...

637
00:21:41,860 --> 00:21:42,950
Little Tangkwa...

638
00:21:43,410 --> 00:21:44,440
Tangkwa...

639
00:21:44,450 --> 00:21:45,240
Oh, he's talking in his sleep.

640
00:21:45,490 --> 00:21:46,360
Who is Tangkwa?

641
00:21:46,360 --> 00:21:47,160
I don't know either.

642
00:21:48,960 --> 00:21:50,570
- Whoa. That's loud.
- ♫Starfish kiss♫

643
00:21:50,580 --> 00:21:51,590
♫Starfish kiss♫

644
00:21:51,600 --> 00:21:52,660
They're doing it at night, too.

645
00:21:52,670 --> 00:21:54,460
♫Kitty kiss♫

646
00:21:54,470 --> 00:21:56,100
♫Starfish kiss♫

647
00:21:56,110 --> 00:21:58,110
♫Starfish kiss♫

648
00:21:59,680 --> 00:22:01,300
♫Goldfish kiss♫

649
00:22:01,310 --> 00:22:03,470
♫All kisses for you♫

650
00:22:10,100 --> 00:22:11,300
This room again?

651
00:22:11,490 --> 00:22:12,600
They're even louder than the last time.

652
00:22:12,600 --> 00:22:13,940
No matter how many times I knocked,
they wouldn't open.

653
00:22:14,520 --> 00:22:15,410
Danis, move.

654
00:22:15,620 --> 00:22:16,000
Whoa.

655
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:17,120
- Huh?
- I'll break the door down.

656
00:22:17,480 --> 00:22:17,960
Huh?!

657
00:22:18,080 --> 00:22:18,950
Three...

658
00:22:19,430 --> 00:22:20,220
Two...

659
00:22:20,490 --> 00:22:21,050
One.

660
00:22:22,410 --> 00:22:23,240
- Whoa!
- Whoa!

661
00:22:23,940 --> 00:22:25,370
Hey, are you alright?

662
00:22:25,530 --> 00:22:25,940
Hey!

663
00:22:27,150 --> 00:22:29,460
Am I really seeing a police officer
slipping and sliding

664
00:22:29,480 --> 00:22:31,380
over there...?

665
00:22:33,800 --> 00:22:34,550
Get up.

666
00:22:34,550 --> 00:22:35,040
Are you okay?

667
00:22:35,040 --> 00:22:36,050
I'm fine.

668
00:22:36,060 --> 00:22:36,630
Hey...

669
00:22:37,240 --> 00:22:38,320
You opened the door
without warning.

670
00:22:40,240 --> 00:22:41,400
Hey,

671
00:22:41,610 --> 00:22:43,300
didn't you say you'd keep it down?

672
00:22:43,660 --> 00:22:44,830
You said you'd sing cute songs.

673
00:22:44,960 --> 00:22:45,720
Yeah.

674
00:22:45,730 --> 00:22:46,890
This is the same song.

675
00:22:47,080 --> 00:22:48,570
The "JuBu Jub" song we told you.

676
00:22:48,760 --> 00:22:50,040
It's just a bit more hardcore.

677
00:22:50,050 --> 00:22:50,660
How?

678
00:22:50,940 --> 00:22:52,980
♫Goose kiss♫

679
00:22:52,980 --> 00:22:54,700
♫Starfish kiss♫

680
00:22:54,700 --> 00:22:56,480
- ♫Goldfish kiss♫
- Hey!

681
00:22:56,480 --> 00:22:57,050
Hey!

682
00:22:57,050 --> 00:22:58,300
♫Rooster kiss♫

683
00:22:58,300 --> 00:23:02,730
♫All kisses for you♫

684
00:23:03,020 --> 00:23:03,920
Ugh!

685
00:23:04,120 --> 00:23:05,020
Be quiet!!

686
00:23:06,600 --> 00:23:07,790
I told you to stop them,

687
00:23:08,150 --> 00:23:09,410
but you played along again!

688
00:23:10,680 --> 00:23:11,600
Stop! I said stop!

689
00:23:12,060 --> 00:23:12,720
How could I stop?

690
00:23:12,720 --> 00:23:13,980
He's still stepping on my foot.

691
00:23:13,980 --> 00:23:14,900
Oh... Oops.

692
00:23:15,480 --> 00:23:16,320
Ugh...

693
00:23:16,330 --> 00:23:19,600
I was about to hear them say, "Giraffe kiss."

694
00:23:21,800 --> 00:23:22,550
Hey,

695
00:23:23,100 --> 00:23:24,760
you won't listen when
I talk to you nicely,

696
00:23:24,760 --> 00:23:25,400
huh?

697
00:23:28,380 --> 00:23:29,370
What about it?

698
00:23:34,300 --> 00:23:35,560
You're all grown ass high schoolers.

699
00:23:35,560 --> 00:23:36,950
Learn some manners, won't you?

700
00:23:36,950 --> 00:23:37,830
Ooh...

701
00:23:37,960 --> 00:23:39,850
This is a shared space,
not a private one.

702
00:23:39,850 --> 00:23:41,520
Learn to think of others.

703
00:23:41,520 --> 00:23:43,150
Don't be so selfish. Do you understand?

704
00:23:43,150 --> 00:23:44,320
But we...

705
00:23:44,320 --> 00:23:45,040
Shut up!

706
00:23:45,040 --> 00:23:46,170
The adult is talking. Do not interrupt me.

707
00:23:46,170 --> 00:23:47,710
Didn't anyone teach you this?

708
00:23:47,720 --> 00:23:48,950
Didn't your parents teach you manners?

709
00:23:48,950 --> 00:23:50,410
I'll teach you myself, then.

710
00:23:50,410 --> 00:23:52,000
Think of your parents when you do things.

711
00:23:52,000 --> 00:23:53,750
Then when people insult you,
your parents won't be dragged into it.

712
00:23:53,750 --> 00:23:55,300
They sent you here to study,
not to act like assholes.

713
00:23:55,300 --> 00:23:55,920
Do you understand?

714
00:23:56,850 --> 00:23:58,840
Who do you think you are to lecture us?

715
00:23:58,850 --> 00:23:59,570
That's right!

716
00:23:59,580 --> 00:24:00,490
Didn't your school teach you?!

717
00:24:00,490 --> 00:24:01,570
This is a dorm.

718
00:24:01,690 --> 00:24:03,090
If you can't keep it down,

719
00:24:03,100 --> 00:24:04,780
then go live at home!

720
00:24:04,890 --> 00:24:06,170
Dobby, why are you quiet?

721
00:24:06,170 --> 00:24:07,370
Help me out. Say something, will you?

722
00:24:07,370 --> 00:24:08,540
Dobby, can you hear me?!

723
00:24:08,540 --> 00:24:09,100
Ugh...

724
00:24:09,100 --> 00:24:11,230
You've said it all. I don't need to say
anything anymore.

725
00:24:11,610 --> 00:24:12,950
Scolding them is a waste of time.

726
00:24:13,340 --> 00:24:14,710
Just kick all three of them out!

727
00:24:14,730 --> 00:24:15,620
- Yeah!
- What?

728
00:24:15,620 --> 00:24:16,850
You can't do that.

729
00:24:16,980 --> 00:24:17,750
You want problems, huh?!

730
00:24:17,760 --> 00:24:19,400
- Whoa!
- Hey... Calm down, Dump.

731
00:24:20,640 --> 00:24:22,000
There's a reason

732
00:24:22,010 --> 00:24:22,890
we were so loud.

733
00:24:22,900 --> 00:24:23,730
What is it?

734
00:24:24,710 --> 00:24:25,970
We...

735
00:24:26,850 --> 00:24:27,850
We were scared...

736
00:24:29,750 --> 00:24:30,480
Scared of what?

737
00:24:32,180 --> 00:24:33,120
We were scared of Gramps' ghost!

738
00:24:33,460 --> 00:24:34,380
- Whoa!
- Huh?!

739
00:24:37,990 --> 00:24:39,000
Not me...

740
00:24:39,220 --> 00:24:39,730
What?

741
00:24:40,050 --> 00:24:41,000
Well, Gramps' ghost

742
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:42,750
haunted us in our dreams.

743
00:24:42,750 --> 00:24:43,380
True.

744
00:24:46,010 --> 00:24:46,830
No, I did not!

745
00:24:47,010 --> 00:24:48,950
When did I even do that?

746
00:24:49,180 --> 00:24:50,890
That was not me. I did not do it!

747
00:24:52,200 --> 00:24:53,680
Don't use Gramps' ghost as an excuse.

748
00:24:53,920 --> 00:24:54,730
Why not?

749
00:24:55,100 --> 00:24:55,940
Gramps even...

750
00:24:55,950 --> 00:24:57,780
visited your mom in her dreams
and told her about the lottery.

751
00:24:58,080 --> 00:24:59,600
So why couldn't he haunt us
in our dreams, too?

752
00:24:59,620 --> 00:25:00,240
That's right!

753
00:25:00,560 --> 00:25:02,460
See, he haunts us every night.
We couldn't sleep.

754
00:25:02,550 --> 00:25:04,000
We're the victims here,

755
00:25:04,100 --> 00:25:05,770
so how can you kick us out?!

756
00:25:06,060 --> 00:25:08,540
- Yeah.
- Be grateful we haven't told our parents.

757
00:25:08,590 --> 00:25:09,540
- Get out! Go!
- Yeah!

758
00:25:09,540 --> 00:25:09,940
Leave.

759
00:25:09,950 --> 00:25:11,170
- Go, go, go.
- Guys, calm down.

760
00:25:11,180 --> 00:25:13,000
- Shouldn't a police officer be catching criminals?
- Get out already.

761
00:25:13,010 --> 00:25:14,410
- Leave us.
- Go away.

762
00:25:14,420 --> 00:25:15,350
- Get out of here.
- Hey...

763
00:25:15,350 --> 00:25:16,550
- Don't use Grandpa's ghost as an excuse!
- Let's talk.

764
00:25:16,550 --> 00:25:18,550
- Get out! Leave!
- Don't push me, hey!

765
00:25:18,660 --> 00:25:19,240
Hey.

766
00:25:19,530 --> 00:25:20,730
These kids!

767
00:25:20,730 --> 00:25:21,920
I even brought a police officer with me,

768
00:25:21,920 --> 00:25:23,520
but it didn't seem to help at all.

769
00:25:23,520 --> 00:25:24,820
Well... Even if I arrested them,

770
00:25:24,820 --> 00:25:26,490
the police could only fine and
give them a warning.

771
00:25:26,500 --> 00:25:27,840
They'd just be allowed to go home.

772
00:25:29,100 --> 00:25:29,890
I don't think fining them

773
00:25:29,900 --> 00:25:31,210
is enough to make them learn a lesson.

774
00:25:31,500 --> 00:25:33,320
They used Grandpa's ghost
as an excuse, huh?

775
00:25:34,780 --> 00:25:35,750
Fine!

776
00:25:35,750 --> 00:25:37,400
We'll see about this!

777
00:25:45,130 --> 00:25:46,010
So scary...

778
00:25:56,150 --> 00:25:57,220
Hey... What?

779
00:25:58,060 --> 00:25:59,750
Everyone, keep it down.

780
00:26:00,660 --> 00:26:01,460
Under this cardboard box,

781
00:26:01,460 --> 00:26:03,640
there is a black dog with
newborn pups.

782
00:26:04,360 --> 00:26:06,020
I'm still wondering

783
00:26:06,130 --> 00:26:07,420
how to get her tears?

784
00:26:08,960 --> 00:26:10,680
Maybe put on a sad episode from
'Love Upon a Time'?

785
00:26:11,750 --> 00:26:12,950
If you're just going to be annoying,

786
00:26:13,070 --> 00:26:13,860
then keep quiet.

787
00:26:13,870 --> 00:26:14,780
Stop talking.

788
00:26:15,460 --> 00:26:16,550
Be serious.

789
00:26:17,290 --> 00:26:18,720
Getting her tears is easy.

790
00:26:19,340 --> 00:26:20,760
We only have to take one of her pups.

791
00:26:21,170 --> 00:26:22,720
And when the pup wakes up
and doesn't see its mother,

792
00:26:22,730 --> 00:26:23,920
it will cry out,

793
00:26:23,920 --> 00:26:24,950
"Mama!"

794
00:26:25,110 --> 00:26:26,120
We'll get the tears that way.

795
00:26:26,360 --> 00:26:28,040
- Whoa...
- Yeah!

796
00:26:28,240 --> 00:26:29,040
Hey,

797
00:26:29,040 --> 00:26:30,990
you're evil to the core, Guard Dum.

798
00:26:31,330 --> 00:26:32,440
I'll take that as a compliment.

799
00:26:38,150 --> 00:26:38,740
Whoa...

800
00:26:40,440 --> 00:26:41,750
From the direction of her tail,

801
00:26:41,960 --> 00:26:43,580
she's probably facing that way.

802
00:26:44,400 --> 00:26:46,160
And her pups are probably cuddling over here.

803
00:26:46,820 --> 00:26:49,780
I want one brave volunteer

804
00:26:50,580 --> 00:26:51,600
who will take one of the pups out.

805
00:26:51,750 --> 00:26:53,460
If you volunteer, please step forward.

806
00:26:56,280 --> 00:26:56,820
Wow...

807
00:26:56,820 --> 00:26:57,910
You're very brave, Mr. Drip.

808
00:26:59,540 --> 00:27:00,140
What?!

809
00:27:00,140 --> 00:27:00,770
Whoa!

810
00:27:01,900 --> 00:27:02,910
I didn't volunteer,

811
00:27:02,910 --> 00:27:04,030
and I didn't step forward.

812
00:27:04,330 --> 00:27:05,180
It's alright.

813
00:27:05,300 --> 00:27:06,400
If I could do it, I would.

814
00:27:06,410 --> 00:27:08,280
But I couldn't bend over because of my belly.

815
00:27:08,640 --> 00:27:09,600
Come on... This way.

816
00:27:09,800 --> 00:27:10,550
You're amazing.

817
00:27:10,550 --> 00:27:11,460
I'm impressed.

818
00:27:11,580 --> 00:27:12,540
Go on. She's right there.

819
00:27:12,540 --> 00:27:13,820
Go ahead, Mr. Drip.

820
00:27:13,820 --> 00:27:14,890
It's not scary.

821
00:27:17,260 --> 00:27:18,210
Go on. Over there.

822
00:27:18,650 --> 00:27:20,150
Do you really think I'm
brave enough for this?

823
00:27:20,170 --> 00:27:21,020
It's going to be fine.

824
00:27:33,600 --> 00:27:34,290
Found it.

825
00:27:34,520 --> 00:27:35,490
- Whoa!
- Wow...

826
00:27:35,700 --> 00:27:36,620
The dog's hair is pretty long.

827
00:27:36,620 --> 00:27:37,920
I think this is a poodle.

828
00:27:38,150 --> 00:27:38,850
Yeah...

829
00:27:38,850 --> 00:27:39,770
This breed is friendly.

830
00:27:41,870 --> 00:27:43,220
It's balding here.

831
00:27:44,020 --> 00:27:45,350
Probably scabies.

832
00:27:46,550 --> 00:27:47,750
Poor thing...

833
00:27:50,800 --> 00:27:52,250
There's something long here.

834
00:27:54,230 --> 00:27:55,300
This one might be a male pup.

835
00:27:55,840 --> 00:27:57,960
- Oh...
- I see...

836
00:27:58,490 --> 00:27:59,330
And...

837
00:28:01,330 --> 00:28:02,330
Seems like there's a hole, too.

838
00:28:02,340 --> 00:28:03,350
Ugh!

839
00:28:04,080 --> 00:28:05,130
You don't need to describe it anymore.

840
00:28:05,450 --> 00:28:06,560
Just take it out already.

841
00:28:07,180 --> 00:28:07,800
Alright.

842
00:28:08,760 --> 00:28:09,060
Oh!

843
00:28:09,060 --> 00:28:10,130
- Ow!
- Whoa, whoa!

844
00:28:10,130 --> 00:28:10,880
Hey, hey, hey!

845
00:28:10,880 --> 00:28:12,570
- It bit me!
- Help him!

846
00:28:12,570 --> 00:28:13,180
- Ouch...
- Hey!

847
00:28:13,460 --> 00:28:14,300
Ow, help me!

848
00:28:20,960 --> 00:28:22,400
Ouch!

849
00:28:23,140 --> 00:28:23,750
Mr. Drip!

850
00:28:24,080 --> 00:28:24,950
Are you hurt, Mr. Drip?!

851
00:28:25,880 --> 00:28:26,580
Ugh!!

852
00:28:27,280 --> 00:28:28,800
It hurts because of you, Mr. Dolly!

853
00:28:30,250 --> 00:28:30,950
Hey, wait...

854
00:28:32,150 --> 00:28:34,210
Why does it look nothing
like a dog bite?

855
00:28:34,210 --> 00:28:35,640
It looks like a human bite mark.

856
00:28:35,720 --> 00:28:36,330
Ugh!

857
00:28:37,250 --> 00:28:38,410
Well, I am a human!

858
00:28:39,160 --> 00:28:40,170
What the heck are you doing here?!

859
00:28:40,200 --> 00:28:40,760
Whoa...

860
00:28:40,760 --> 00:28:41,380
Huh?!

861
00:28:42,260 --> 00:28:42,820
Who?

862
00:28:42,820 --> 00:28:43,830
Who came up with this idea?

863
00:28:43,860 --> 00:28:44,780
- This guy right here.
- He did.

864
00:28:48,770 --> 00:28:49,950
Come here, chubby.

865
00:28:50,290 --> 00:28:51,480
You'll take me to the hospital.

866
00:28:51,480 --> 00:28:51,880
Why?

867
00:28:51,880 --> 00:28:53,900
Your friend hurt my head lice!

868
00:28:54,530 --> 00:28:57,280
What did you do to my
Mojo Dojo Casa House?

869
00:28:57,280 --> 00:28:58,780
I'm sorry... Mister...

870
00:28:58,780 --> 00:29:00,000
Do you know who I am?

871
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:00,720
No?

872
00:29:00,720 --> 00:29:02,760
My name is Mister Hasamada Urukamahn

873
00:29:02,760 --> 00:29:03,610
An Incarnation

874
00:29:03,610 --> 00:29:04,460
Who Comes With Explosions

875
00:29:04,470 --> 00:29:05,460
John Weed Puller

876
00:29:05,460 --> 00:29:05,900
Da...

877
00:29:05,900 --> 00:29:06,800
Dafoe?

878
00:29:06,800 --> 00:29:07,520
Da hell.

879
00:29:07,520 --> 00:29:08,410
Whoa!

880
00:29:08,640 --> 00:29:09,310
- Come here.
- Hey!

881
00:29:09,320 --> 00:29:10,330
- Wait, wait.
- Hey!

882
00:29:10,340 --> 00:29:11,750
And who said I'm a poodle?

883
00:29:12,810 --> 00:29:13,930
I'm a Siberian husky!

884
00:29:13,930 --> 00:29:15,120
Whoa! Chill, bro!

885
00:29:16,500 --> 00:29:19,200
[The D Dorm]

886
00:29:19,570 --> 00:29:20,000
Ugh...

887
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:21,800
Who is making noises
so early in the morning?

888
00:29:24,020 --> 00:29:24,620
What?

889
00:29:25,090 --> 00:29:26,410
Good job, Auntie Duang.

890
00:29:27,050 --> 00:29:28,550
Why is she dancing here?

891
00:29:29,010 --> 00:29:30,220
We're trying to sleep here.

892
00:29:34,000 --> 00:29:35,950
I'm doing this for your sake.

893
00:29:36,080 --> 00:29:37,170
Since you said that...

894
00:29:37,170 --> 00:29:39,170
Grandpa's ghost liked to
haunt you at night, right?

895
00:29:39,170 --> 00:29:40,630
You couldn't sleep at all, yeah?

896
00:29:40,810 --> 00:29:42,120
That's why I hired Auntie Duang

897
00:29:42,310 --> 00:29:43,780
to come dance for Grandpa's ghost,

898
00:29:43,980 --> 00:29:45,810
so he wouldn't disturb you at night.

899
00:29:46,770 --> 00:29:48,090
Gramps!

900
00:29:48,090 --> 00:29:50,480
Come watch me dance,
and don't scare the kids, alright?

901
00:29:50,480 --> 00:29:51,920
- Yeah, I am watching you.
- Understood?

902
00:29:51,920 --> 00:29:52,760
Got it.

903
00:29:52,760 --> 00:29:53,640
Leave.

904
00:29:53,640 --> 00:29:54,180
Shoo!

905
00:29:54,180 --> 00:29:54,950
Ow...

906
00:29:54,950 --> 00:29:56,620
- Shoo!
- Keep going.

907
00:29:56,620 --> 00:29:57,820
- Shoo!
- Ow!

908
00:29:57,820 --> 00:29:58,370
Good.

909
00:29:58,370 --> 00:29:59,750
Hey, Auntie!

910
00:30:00,080 --> 00:30:01,830
Are you trying to banish us
instead of the ghost?!

911
00:30:02,150 --> 00:30:02,850
Would you like this, then?!

912
00:30:02,850 --> 00:30:04,400
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

913
00:30:05,100 --> 00:30:06,950
Are you trying to get back at us?

914
00:30:07,490 --> 00:30:08,600
Wow...

915
00:30:08,760 --> 00:30:10,700
That boy is always so jumpy.

916
00:30:10,700 --> 00:30:12,110
That boy is always so sippy.

917
00:30:12,520 --> 00:30:14,670
How are you not annoyed by each other?

918
00:30:15,350 --> 00:30:16,450
Hey, guys...

919
00:30:16,550 --> 00:30:18,550
If we really were trying to
get back at you...

920
00:30:19,110 --> 00:30:20,900
What about it, then?

921
00:30:21,010 --> 00:30:21,960
Hm?!

922
00:30:21,960 --> 00:30:23,000
Now you'll understand

923
00:30:23,000 --> 00:30:24,240
how it feels like to be disturbed.

924
00:30:24,240 --> 00:30:26,200
I'll give you some advice.
If you can't live like this,

925
00:30:26,200 --> 00:30:27,310
then leave!

926
00:30:27,310 --> 00:30:28,360
- All three of you.
- Never!

927
00:30:29,300 --> 00:30:30,560
You are the ones that need to leave.

928
00:30:31,600 --> 00:30:32,840
Leave, leave, leave.

929
00:30:32,840 --> 00:30:33,890
- Go, go, go, go.
- Whoa, whoa, whoa.

930
00:30:33,890 --> 00:30:34,540
Guys.

931
00:30:34,680 --> 00:30:35,750
- Hey, are you asking for trouble?
- Go, go, go, go.

932
00:30:35,750 --> 00:30:36,810
How dare you hurt her?

933
00:30:36,810 --> 00:30:37,990
Whoever picks a fight with me,

934
00:30:38,000 --> 00:30:39,010
I don't discriminate.

935
00:30:39,010 --> 00:30:39,700
Hey, you can't do that.

936
00:30:39,700 --> 00:30:40,200
Step back.

937
00:30:40,200 --> 00:30:41,750
Hey, did you push my friend?

938
00:30:41,890 --> 00:30:43,350
- Would you like some of this, then?!
- Whoa, don't do that. Hey!

939
00:30:43,360 --> 00:30:44,390
Bring it on!

940
00:30:47,320 --> 00:30:48,720
Whoa, Auntie Duang!

941
00:30:52,550 --> 00:30:53,700
- Hey!
- Auntie Duang!

942
00:30:53,700 --> 00:30:54,520
Duang...

943
00:30:54,960 --> 00:30:55,740
Oh...

944
00:30:55,740 --> 00:30:56,430
Auntie Duang.

945
00:30:56,600 --> 00:30:57,760
Hey! Don't try to run away!

946
00:30:58,740 --> 00:30:59,330
Stop running...

947
00:30:59,750 --> 00:31:00,570
- Auntie Duang!
- Duang!

948
00:31:00,570 --> 00:31:01,200
Hey!

949
00:31:01,930 --> 00:31:04,680
[The D Dorm]

950
00:31:06,420 --> 00:31:08,150
I couldn't focus on today's lessons at all.

951
00:31:08,910 --> 00:31:09,920
What about you guys?

952
00:31:10,660 --> 00:31:13,380
I just took a peek at
Auntie Duang's restaurant.

953
00:31:13,380 --> 00:31:14,150
How was it?

954
00:31:14,150 --> 00:31:15,350
It was closed.

955
00:31:15,350 --> 00:31:16,010
Huh?

956
00:31:16,510 --> 00:31:17,500
It's never been closed before.

957
00:31:18,100 --> 00:31:18,840
Dape.

958
00:31:18,840 --> 00:31:19,380
Hm?

959
00:31:20,420 --> 00:31:21,860
Aren't you scared?

960
00:31:22,820 --> 00:31:23,750
Scared of what?

961
00:31:25,210 --> 00:31:26,500
If we insisted that

962
00:31:26,510 --> 00:31:27,750
we didn't push her

963
00:31:27,760 --> 00:31:29,120
and that she fell down on her own,

964
00:31:29,880 --> 00:31:33,170
the law would protect
minors like us anyway, right?

965
00:31:37,300 --> 00:31:38,610
So cool.

966
00:31:39,780 --> 00:31:40,790
Besides,

967
00:31:41,890 --> 00:31:42,950
my father can always pull some strings

968
00:31:43,140 --> 00:31:44,520
and get us out of trouble.

969
00:31:44,850 --> 00:31:46,250
Yeah, that's true.

970
00:31:46,940 --> 00:31:48,460
I'm jealous of you, having a father like that.

971
00:31:48,700 --> 00:31:50,400
He's super-duper cool.

972
00:31:51,050 --> 00:31:52,060
That's great, bro.

973
00:31:52,320 --> 00:31:53,340
- Mm.
- Of course.

974
00:31:53,710 --> 00:31:54,730
Come on, let's get on with our band practice.

975
00:31:54,730 --> 00:31:55,830
Hey, guys...

976
00:31:55,830 --> 00:31:56,570
Hm?

977
00:31:56,930 --> 00:31:58,220
What is that in front of our room?

978
00:31:58,900 --> 00:31:59,750
Go take a look, won't you?

979
00:32:03,560 --> 00:32:04,370
What?

980
00:32:04,370 --> 00:32:06,370
[You are cordially invited to the bathing rite of
Mrs. Duangjai Rungthiwahong (Auntie Duang)]

981
00:32:06,370 --> 00:32:08,400
Auntie Duang is dead?!

982
00:32:09,840 --> 00:32:10,620
Sh*t!

983
00:32:10,740 --> 00:32:11,750
Dape, it's your fault!

984
00:32:12,620 --> 00:32:13,360
Auntie Duang is dead...

985
00:32:13,360 --> 00:32:14,150
Did we kill her?

986
00:32:14,150 --> 00:32:15,350
What are you afraid of?

987
00:32:15,520 --> 00:32:17,020
I told you. We won't be punished.

988
00:32:17,040 --> 00:32:18,830
But Auntie Duang died for real, though.

989
00:32:19,450 --> 00:32:20,780
Listen to me.

990
00:32:21,060 --> 00:32:24,150
"Juvenile offenders can never be
severely punished."

991
00:32:25,580 --> 00:32:27,730
If they're going to punish us,
my father can take care of it.

992
00:32:27,840 --> 00:32:29,240
We won't get thrown in jail.

993
00:32:33,870 --> 00:32:34,820
Whoa!

994
00:32:35,500 --> 00:32:36,410
Whoa!

995
00:32:38,860 --> 00:32:39,690
Whoa!

996
00:32:39,690 --> 00:32:40,550
Whoa!

997
00:32:40,920 --> 00:32:41,580
Whoa!

998
00:32:41,580 --> 00:32:43,450
Who the hell put Thai music on?!

999
00:32:43,710 --> 00:32:45,160
Is it Auntie Duang's ghost?!

1000
00:32:45,490 --> 00:32:47,170
Ugh, stop making such a fuss!

1001
00:32:48,400 --> 00:32:49,490
Who is behind this?!

1002
00:32:49,490 --> 00:32:50,440
Show yourself!

1003
00:32:51,140 --> 00:32:51,660
There...

1004
00:32:51,660 --> 00:32:53,120
There she comes...

1005
00:32:53,130 --> 00:32:54,000
Dape...

1006
00:32:54,820 --> 00:32:56,660
You can stay here if you want!

1007
00:32:56,960 --> 00:32:57,960
We're...

1008
00:32:57,960 --> 00:32:58,810
leaving!

1009
00:33:00,370 --> 00:33:01,150
Come back here.

1010
00:33:02,530 --> 00:33:03,370
Come back.

1011
00:33:04,410 --> 00:33:05,570
Come back here!

1012
00:33:11,520 --> 00:33:12,950
If you're not coming back...

1013
00:33:14,540 --> 00:33:15,690
then wait for me.

1014
00:33:16,090 --> 00:33:17,210
Wait for me!

1015
00:33:19,300 --> 00:33:20,020
Whoa...

1016
00:33:20,150 --> 00:33:21,650
Why did you guys stop?

1017
00:33:23,120 --> 00:33:24,370
Look...

1018
00:33:24,370 --> 00:33:25,350
- Whoa!
- Auntie Duang's ghost...

1019
00:33:26,000 --> 00:33:27,000
Auntie Duang's ghost...

1020
00:33:31,720 --> 00:33:33,200
Auntie, I'm sorry!

1021
00:33:34,250 --> 00:33:35,920
These two pushed you down the stairs.

1022
00:33:35,920 --> 00:33:36,650
- Huh?
- Huh?

1023
00:33:37,520 --> 00:33:38,150
I didn't do it.

1024
00:33:38,150 --> 00:33:39,160
I was drinking...

1025
00:33:39,160 --> 00:33:40,940
I was drinking a cola, Auntie.

1026
00:33:41,300 --> 00:33:42,850
Dope! What are you saying?

1027
00:33:43,090 --> 00:33:45,040
You guys apologize to Auntie right now!

1028
00:33:46,040 --> 00:33:47,170
I... I have nothing to do with this.

1029
00:33:47,170 --> 00:33:48,020
I'm going that way.

1030
00:33:48,340 --> 00:33:49,640
Hey, I'm coming with you!

1031
00:33:53,200 --> 00:33:53,740
What?

1032
00:33:53,750 --> 00:33:54,830
What? Why did you stop?

1033
00:33:55,540 --> 00:33:57,040
She doesn't have a head...

1034
00:34:00,240 --> 00:34:00,950
Dump,

1035
00:34:01,220 --> 00:34:02,320
you like jumping at people, right?

1036
00:34:02,520 --> 00:34:03,180
Huh?

1037
00:34:03,350 --> 00:34:04,550
Bring it on!

1038
00:34:05,100 --> 00:34:06,370
Don't!

1039
00:34:07,050 --> 00:34:08,139
Bring it on!

1040
00:34:08,150 --> 00:34:09,389
Don't bring it on!

1041
00:34:09,800 --> 00:34:10,409
Ugh...

1042
00:34:10,620 --> 00:34:12,010
Bring it on! Come on!

1043
00:34:12,010 --> 00:34:13,300
Don't!

1044
00:34:13,610 --> 00:34:14,980
Don't...

1045
00:34:16,210 --> 00:34:17,699
I'll get there myself!

1046
00:34:24,949 --> 00:34:25,960
I'm... I'm sorry.

1047
00:34:26,290 --> 00:34:26,850
I'm sorry...

1048
00:34:26,850 --> 00:34:27,350
I...

1049
00:34:29,750 --> 00:34:30,949
I... I didn't mean to do it.

1050
00:34:30,949 --> 00:34:33,199
Dump... Dump bumped into me.

1051
00:34:33,350 --> 00:34:33,909
What?

1052
00:34:33,909 --> 00:34:34,929
Why the hell are you blaming me?!

1053
00:34:34,940 --> 00:34:36,010
Auntie, listen...

1054
00:34:36,010 --> 00:34:37,330
He's the worst.

1055
00:34:37,340 --> 00:34:39,010
He said we'd never get sent to jail

1056
00:34:39,010 --> 00:34:40,550
because we're juvenile offenders.

1057
00:34:40,679 --> 00:34:42,070
Even if we went to jail,
his father would help us out.

1058
00:34:42,070 --> 00:34:43,179
Break his neck, Auntie!

1059
00:34:43,320 --> 00:34:44,699
Snap it!

1060
00:34:44,699 --> 00:34:46,219
Snap his neck...

1061
00:34:46,400 --> 00:34:48,350
I'll kill you all!

1062
00:34:48,480 --> 00:34:49,130
Don't!

1063
00:34:49,130 --> 00:34:50,370
- No!
- Don't!

1064
00:34:51,010 --> 00:34:52,139
- No...
- No! Don't!

1065
00:34:54,520 --> 00:34:56,610
We're doomed.

1066
00:34:56,610 --> 00:34:58,040
We're done for...

1067
00:34:58,040 --> 00:34:59,750
Tada!

1068
00:34:59,920 --> 00:35:02,190
Auntie Duang is not dead, you minors.

1069
00:35:07,420 --> 00:35:08,410
Tada!

1070
00:35:08,410 --> 00:35:09,190
Whoa!

1071
00:35:16,090 --> 00:35:17,300
Humans are better than ghosts

1072
00:35:17,330 --> 00:35:19,240
when it comes to scaring fellow humans, huh?

1073
00:35:20,930 --> 00:35:22,590
You pranked us?!

1074
00:35:25,920 --> 00:35:27,680
I won't let this slide.

1075
00:35:27,940 --> 00:35:30,500
I'll have my father close your dorm down!

1076
00:35:34,440 --> 00:35:38,520
[The D Dorm]

1077
00:35:39,220 --> 00:35:41,360
I already took care of
the ingredients that would expire soon.

1078
00:35:42,370 --> 00:35:43,730
Get some rest, Mr. Drip.

1079
00:35:43,730 --> 00:35:44,870
Don't worry about the cafe.

1080
00:35:45,220 --> 00:35:46,630
Focus on your recovery for now.

1081
00:35:47,640 --> 00:35:48,380
Yes.

1082
00:35:50,620 --> 00:35:51,350
By the way...

1083
00:35:52,280 --> 00:35:53,290
Mr. Dobby and the others...

1084
00:35:53,300 --> 00:35:55,720
They didn't prank
those kids too harshly, did they?

1085
00:35:57,240 --> 00:35:58,750
They deserved worse than that

1086
00:35:59,320 --> 00:36:01,010
for pushing my mom down the stairs.

1087
00:36:01,570 --> 00:36:03,580
She's lucky that she has a very flexible

1088
00:36:03,580 --> 00:36:05,240
and stout body with a thick neck,

1089
00:36:05,240 --> 00:36:06,450
so she wasn't severely injured.

1090
00:36:06,450 --> 00:36:07,870
A stout body with a thick neck?

1091
00:36:08,600 --> 00:36:09,940
Your mother has a funny body shape.

1092
00:36:09,940 --> 00:36:10,530
Hey!

1093
00:36:10,530 --> 00:36:11,240
Just like me...

1094
00:36:12,230 --> 00:36:12,950
It's alright.

1095
00:36:13,600 --> 00:36:15,350
Hey, about what you said earlier,
you don't have to worry.

1096
00:36:15,350 --> 00:36:16,180
Mr. Dollar was there, too.

1097
00:36:16,180 --> 00:36:18,090
He wouldn't let them get hurt.

1098
00:36:18,090 --> 00:36:18,720
That's right...

1099
00:36:19,120 --> 00:36:20,150
The person you should

1100
00:36:20,320 --> 00:36:21,310
be worried about is Mr. Drip.

1101
00:36:21,990 --> 00:36:23,660
He fell down a sewer while running
from that madman.

1102
00:36:24,020 --> 00:36:25,760
I can't say when he'll be able to
open the cafe again.

1103
00:36:26,380 --> 00:36:27,140
Are you worried about him?

1104
00:36:32,380 --> 00:36:33,410
Ahem...

1105
00:36:33,740 --> 00:36:34,250
Oh...

1106
00:36:35,290 --> 00:36:35,860
- I got it!
- Whoa!

1107
00:36:35,870 --> 00:36:36,470
Whoa...

1108
00:36:36,990 --> 00:36:38,000
A black dog's tears.

1109
00:36:38,500 --> 00:36:40,670
Don't tell me you fought a dog for that?

1110
00:36:41,430 --> 00:36:42,260
Ugh...

1111
00:36:42,260 --> 00:36:43,370
Why were you so hell-bent on getting that?

1112
00:36:43,530 --> 00:36:44,610
This time,

1113
00:36:44,960 --> 00:36:46,140
I'll finally be able to see ghosts.

1114
00:36:48,800 --> 00:36:49,600
- Hey...
- Oh, oh.

1115
00:36:50,600 --> 00:36:51,170
Whoa...

1116
00:36:58,880 --> 00:36:59,750
Gah...

1117
00:37:00,040 --> 00:37:00,950
- Whoa.
- Gah...

1118
00:37:01,210 --> 00:37:02,570
I think it worked. He's seeing something.

1119
00:37:02,590 --> 00:37:03,700
- Gah!
- "Gramps"?

1120
00:37:03,700 --> 00:37:04,700
Where is he?

1121
00:37:06,950 --> 00:37:07,760
It burns!

1122
00:37:07,760 --> 00:37:08,150
What?

1123
00:37:08,150 --> 00:37:08,860
What?

1124
00:37:08,860 --> 00:37:10,380
Hey, he needs some water.

1125
00:37:10,380 --> 00:37:11,370
- Help him...
- I'll help.

1126
00:37:11,370 --> 00:37:12,270
What's wrong?

1127
00:37:12,270 --> 00:37:13,280
Take me to the doctor...

1128
00:37:13,780 --> 00:37:14,920
Don't touch me! Move!

1129
00:37:21,500 --> 00:37:24,700
I want to see what their parents look like.

1130
00:37:24,700 --> 00:37:26,150
These kids...

1131
00:37:26,150 --> 00:37:27,680
How were they even raised

1132
00:37:27,680 --> 00:37:30,680
to become such a menace to society?

1133
00:37:31,140 --> 00:37:31,850
Who?!

1134
00:37:32,400 --> 00:37:33,350
Who did this?!

1135
00:37:37,220 --> 00:37:39,220
Who dared pick on my son?

1136
00:37:39,460 --> 00:37:40,010
Huh?

1137
00:37:40,550 --> 00:37:41,380
Wow...

1138
00:37:41,750 --> 00:37:43,220
Acting all high and mighty.

1139
00:37:43,490 --> 00:37:45,350
No wonder your son
turned out that way.

1140
00:37:49,220 --> 00:37:50,000
What even are you?

1141
00:37:50,290 --> 00:37:50,970
A kappa.

1142
00:37:50,970 --> 00:37:51,630
I'm not leaving.

1143
00:37:51,630 --> 00:37:52,550
I just got here.

1144
00:37:53,210 --> 00:37:54,950
Everyone here

1145
00:37:55,340 --> 00:37:57,110
humiliated my son.

1146
00:37:57,490 --> 00:37:58,550
You'll have to be responsible for this!

1147
00:37:59,600 --> 00:38:01,620
Tell Uncle Danai who owns this
dorm to come talk to me.

1148
00:38:03,710 --> 00:38:05,200
You know my Grandpa?

1149
00:38:05,790 --> 00:38:06,990
Stop talking

1150
00:38:07,330 --> 00:38:09,110
and bring him here already!

1151
00:38:10,640 --> 00:38:11,730
Surachet?

1152
00:38:12,050 --> 00:38:12,720
Is it...

1153
00:38:12,840 --> 00:38:14,580
Is it really you...?

1154
00:38:16,400 --> 00:38:17,750
My Grandpa passed away.

1155
00:38:18,400 --> 00:38:19,600
I'm now in charge of this property.

1156
00:38:19,860 --> 00:38:20,920
You can talk to me.

1157
00:38:21,110 --> 00:38:23,310
These kids were just a bit too loud.

1158
00:38:23,560 --> 00:38:25,260
Just a warning should've been enough,

1159
00:38:25,620 --> 00:38:27,820
but you tried to scare them with ghosts.

1160
00:38:28,100 --> 00:38:30,540
If my son had a heart attack,

1161
00:38:30,770 --> 00:38:31,760
who would be responsible for that?!

1162
00:38:32,720 --> 00:38:33,710
Yes, Dad.

1163
00:38:34,210 --> 00:38:35,050
I was scared...

1164
00:38:36,240 --> 00:38:37,380
I was so scared.

1165
00:38:40,680 --> 00:38:41,750
But your son

1166
00:38:42,530 --> 00:38:43,840
pushed my mom down the stairs.

1167
00:38:45,350 --> 00:38:46,880
If something happened to her,

1168
00:38:47,540 --> 00:38:48,580
who would be responsible for that?

1169
00:38:49,190 --> 00:38:50,040
Yes, Dear.

1170
00:38:50,310 --> 00:38:51,160
I was scared...

1171
00:38:51,350 --> 00:38:52,860
I was so scared.

1172
00:38:52,860 --> 00:38:53,750
Ugh...

1173
00:38:53,910 --> 00:38:56,080
You're the scariest person right now.

1174
00:38:56,520 --> 00:38:57,220
Hey...

1175
00:39:00,270 --> 00:39:02,150
Why is he drinking that all day?

1176
00:39:02,150 --> 00:39:03,080
When did he even get a refill?

1177
00:39:03,350 --> 00:39:04,550
Auntie,

1178
00:39:04,630 --> 00:39:06,500
- I apologize on my son's behalf...
- Shut up!

1179
00:39:06,500 --> 00:39:07,120
You...

1180
00:39:10,200 --> 00:39:11,420
Shut your stupid mouth.

1181
00:39:11,790 --> 00:39:12,800
Keep your nose out of this.

1182
00:39:14,820 --> 00:39:15,960
Surachet...

1183
00:39:16,780 --> 00:39:17,750
You...

1184
00:39:28,060 --> 00:39:29,360
How did you know that

1185
00:39:29,820 --> 00:39:32,860
my son was the one who
pushed that auntie, huh?

1186
00:39:33,760 --> 00:39:35,090
My son...

1187
00:39:35,620 --> 00:39:36,760
is a good kid.

1188
00:39:37,250 --> 00:39:38,320
That's true.

1189
00:39:39,160 --> 00:39:39,880
I...

1190
00:39:40,050 --> 00:39:41,390
I couldn't even bring myself
to step on some ants.

1191
00:39:42,480 --> 00:39:43,400
Yesterday...

1192
00:39:43,800 --> 00:39:46,070
I saw an ant nest in the water.

1193
00:39:47,170 --> 00:39:49,850
I...scooped the ants up slowly

1194
00:39:49,850 --> 00:39:51,350
one by one.

1195
00:39:52,740 --> 00:39:54,050
It took me an hour

1196
00:39:54,250 --> 00:39:55,650
to save every single ant.

1197
00:39:57,180 --> 00:39:59,210
Why would you save just one of them at a time?

1198
00:39:59,210 --> 00:40:00,440
Why not just pick up the whole nest?

1199
00:40:01,600 --> 00:40:02,150
Ow...

1200
00:40:03,740 --> 00:40:04,840
There's one of them here.

1201
00:40:07,190 --> 00:40:08,150
Be quiet

1202
00:40:08,680 --> 00:40:09,690
and keep your mouth shut.

1203
00:40:12,360 --> 00:40:13,920
You said that your son was a good person.

1204
00:40:15,140 --> 00:40:16,140
We have evidence against that.

1205
00:40:17,260 --> 00:40:18,040
Where is it?

1206
00:40:18,400 --> 00:40:19,210
Here.

1207
00:40:26,420 --> 00:40:28,550
♫Kiss, kiss, kiss, kiss, kiss♫

1208
00:40:28,550 --> 00:40:29,750
♫This kiss is for you♫

1209
00:40:30,300 --> 00:40:33,000
- ♫Kiss, kiss, kiss, kiss, kiss♫
- Uh... Sorry.

1210
00:40:33,030 --> 00:40:34,400
- Uh...
- Hey... Do it properly.

1211
00:40:34,550 --> 00:40:35,560
You went along with it, too.

1212
00:40:36,940 --> 00:40:37,330
Here.

1213
00:40:37,330 --> 00:40:38,150
I'm sorry!

1214
00:40:38,150 --> 00:40:39,350
I... I didn't mean to do it.

1215
00:40:39,350 --> 00:40:41,710
Dump... Dump bumped into me...

1216
00:40:41,710 --> 00:40:42,220
What?

1217
00:40:42,230 --> 00:40:43,150
Why the hell are you blaming me?!

1218
00:40:43,330 --> 00:40:44,150
Auntie, listen...

1219
00:40:44,150 --> 00:40:45,840
He's the worst.

1220
00:40:45,840 --> 00:40:47,320
He said we'd never get sent to jail

1221
00:40:47,320 --> 00:40:48,890
because we're juvenile offenders.

1222
00:40:48,890 --> 00:40:50,380
Even if we went to jail,
his father would help us out.

1223
00:40:50,380 --> 00:40:51,640
Break his neck, Auntie!

1224
00:40:51,640 --> 00:40:53,000
Snap it!!

1225
00:40:53,000 --> 00:40:54,950
Snap his neck...

1226
00:40:58,800 --> 00:40:59,380
Alright.

1227
00:41:00,580 --> 00:41:02,150
If my son is actually in the wrong...

1228
00:41:03,230 --> 00:41:03,900
Alright, then.

1229
00:41:04,550 --> 00:41:05,750
What do you want?

1230
00:41:06,640 --> 00:41:07,840
A flower basket?

1231
00:41:08,410 --> 00:41:09,420
Money?

1232
00:41:10,140 --> 00:41:11,290
What do you want?

1233
00:41:11,750 --> 00:41:12,180
Hm?

1234
00:41:13,430 --> 00:41:14,980
I want your son to know that

1235
00:41:16,700 --> 00:41:17,840
being a minor

1236
00:41:18,350 --> 00:41:19,920
means you'll have
more chances in court.

1237
00:41:20,550 --> 00:41:22,640
It doesn't allow you to
get away without repercussions.

1238
00:41:24,280 --> 00:41:27,080
And since you, his parents,
couldn't teach him that,

1239
00:41:28,200 --> 00:41:29,700
I'll let the law be his teacher.

1240
00:41:31,130 --> 00:41:33,220
Ooh!

1241
00:41:33,350 --> 00:41:34,970
It's not every day

1242
00:41:34,970 --> 00:41:37,040
that you talk like a police officer.

1243
00:41:37,840 --> 00:41:39,590
I only see you dance
in the community.

1244
00:41:39,740 --> 00:41:41,530
Wiggle, wiggle, wiggle...

1245
00:41:41,530 --> 00:41:42,210
- Wiggle...
- That's true, Mom.

1246
00:41:42,210 --> 00:41:42,810
Yeah.

1247
00:41:43,180 --> 00:41:43,810
Alright, Mom.

1248
00:41:44,180 --> 00:41:44,840
Let's go to the police station.

1249
00:41:45,200 --> 00:41:45,710
Wait.

1250
00:41:45,710 --> 00:41:46,650
I was just teasing you,

1251
00:41:46,800 --> 00:41:48,050
now you're arresting me?

1252
00:41:48,050 --> 00:41:49,280
You'll testify at the station.

1253
00:41:49,280 --> 00:41:50,370
Oh. Umm...

1254
00:41:51,350 --> 00:41:51,760
How would I know...?

1255
00:41:51,760 --> 00:41:53,100
Please come to

1256
00:41:53,360 --> 00:41:54,260
the police station.

1257
00:41:57,220 --> 00:41:58,200
You guys, too.

1258
00:41:58,550 --> 00:41:59,090
Come on.

1259
00:42:05,530 --> 00:42:06,560
Follow me.

1260
00:42:06,560 --> 00:42:07,460
Come here.

1261
00:42:07,600 --> 00:42:08,150
Go.

1262
00:42:12,200 --> 00:42:13,580
Why didn't you ask if I wanted a drink?

1263
00:42:13,580 --> 00:42:14,590
Ask me, too.

1264
00:42:15,000 --> 00:42:15,760
Is it good?

1265
00:42:16,250 --> 00:42:17,750
- I want to drink it, too.
- Hey, don't play along.

1266
00:42:17,880 --> 00:42:18,220
What...?

1267
00:42:18,220 --> 00:42:19,580
- Let them go to the police station.
- But he didn't invite...

1268
00:42:20,150 --> 00:42:21,950
Our dorm is finally

1269
00:42:21,950 --> 00:42:23,530
peaceful.

1270
00:42:23,530 --> 00:42:24,040
Yay...

1271
00:42:24,400 --> 00:42:25,900
Thank you, everyone,

1272
00:42:25,900 --> 00:42:27,350
for this Auntie Duang's ghost plan.

1273
00:42:27,860 --> 00:42:29,980
Apart from Guard Dum, you're the only one

1274
00:42:29,980 --> 00:42:31,380
who could come up with such an evil plan.

1275
00:42:31,380 --> 00:42:32,000
That's right.

1276
00:42:32,260 --> 00:42:33,700
Of course, it's only natural...

1277
00:42:33,700 --> 00:42:34,370
Hey, wait.

1278
00:42:34,990 --> 00:42:36,000
Was that a compliment?

1279
00:42:36,580 --> 00:42:37,080
Well...

1280
00:42:37,080 --> 00:42:38,850
It's up to your interpretation.

1281
00:42:39,350 --> 00:42:40,090
You complimented me, right?

1282
00:42:40,430 --> 00:42:41,250
- You did, right?
- Maybe.

1283
00:42:41,250 --> 00:42:41,980
Maybe I did.

1284
00:42:44,150 --> 00:42:45,340
Those kids deserved it.

1285
00:42:45,370 --> 00:42:46,240
- Dobby.
- Hm?

1286
00:42:46,650 --> 00:42:47,560
How did...

1287
00:42:47,560 --> 00:42:49,340
Surachet and Gramps know each other?

1288
00:42:50,150 --> 00:42:50,900
Oh, you're right.

1289
00:42:51,160 --> 00:42:52,370
- Right...
- I was curious about that, too.

1290
00:42:52,870 --> 00:42:53,750
Let me ask him.

1291
00:42:54,010 --> 00:42:54,950
Grandpa!

1292
00:42:54,950 --> 00:42:55,500
What?

1293
00:42:55,720 --> 00:42:56,610
Grandpa!

1294
00:42:56,970 --> 00:42:57,980
Where did he go?

1295
00:42:59,180 --> 00:43:00,400
Serves you right.

1296
00:43:00,520 --> 00:43:01,860
You were doing just fine

1297
00:43:02,040 --> 00:43:03,850
before you applied those dog tears
to your eyes.

1298
00:43:04,260 --> 00:43:05,240
Those were full of germs.

1299
00:43:05,530 --> 00:43:06,080
You know what?

1300
00:43:06,080 --> 00:43:07,260
It should have made you blind.

1301
00:43:07,260 --> 00:43:08,890
That would stop your obsession
with seeing ghosts.

1302
00:43:11,260 --> 00:43:12,610
If you're not going to help, then go away.

1303
00:43:12,820 --> 00:43:14,150
Stop complaining. It's annoying!

1304
00:43:15,250 --> 00:43:16,550
You're the one to talk.

1305
00:43:16,650 --> 00:43:18,160
You were whimpering like a dog,

1306
00:43:19,280 --> 00:43:19,860
"Ow!

1307
00:43:20,150 --> 00:43:21,180
It burns.

1308
00:43:21,180 --> 00:43:21,720
Ow!

1309
00:43:21,720 --> 00:43:22,690
My eyes...

1310
00:43:22,690 --> 00:43:24,220
Ow, it burns."

1311
00:43:24,400 --> 00:43:24,810
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

1312
00:43:24,810 --> 00:43:25,380
- Whoa!
- Whoa!

1313
00:43:30,980 --> 00:43:32,150
What the hell was that?!

1314
00:43:42,050 --> 00:43:42,950
Thanks...

1315
00:43:51,090 --> 00:43:52,800
If you hadn't run away...

1316
00:43:52,820 --> 00:43:54,920
If you had married Surachet,

1317
00:43:56,190 --> 00:43:59,810
what would your life be like right now?

1318
00:44:03,000 --> 00:44:04,460
- Gramps?!
- Gramps?!

1319
00:44:07,450 --> 00:44:08,540
Is that really you?

1320
00:44:09,040 --> 00:44:11,260
You can see me again?

1321
00:44:16,690 --> 00:44:17,380
Whoa...

1322
00:44:20,140 --> 00:44:20,860
Daeng the Handyman?

1323
00:44:21,160 --> 00:44:21,930
Daeng the Handyman.

1324
00:44:24,280 --> 00:44:24,950
Whoa...

1325
00:44:25,410 --> 00:44:26,150
Gramps?

1326
00:44:27,120 --> 00:44:28,420
Where did he go?

1327
00:44:30,740 --> 00:44:31,720
About the Feng Shui Master...

1328
00:44:31,740 --> 00:44:33,000
I don't think that's necessary.

1329
00:44:33,020 --> 00:44:34,890
You can bring them
here after three months.

1330
00:44:34,910 --> 00:44:36,940
Oh, I wanted to tell you that
I won't be bringing them here anymore.

1331
00:44:36,960 --> 00:44:38,170
Oh, you won't?

1332
00:44:38,200 --> 00:44:40,490
My boss will hire a shaman
to handle this instead.

1333
00:44:40,590 --> 00:44:41,520
Huh?!

1334
00:44:47,630 --> 00:44:49,370
- Can I draw your eyebrows, then?
- Ugh, hey.

1335
00:44:49,400 --> 00:44:50,680
- Why... What are you gonna do?
- These two

1336
00:44:50,770 --> 00:44:51,870
only fight

1337
00:44:51,890 --> 00:44:52,910
when it comes to their father!

1338
00:44:53,220 --> 00:44:54,010
Who are you?

1339
00:44:54,040 --> 00:44:54,470
Oh!

1340
00:44:54,490 --> 00:44:55,940
What are you doing here?

1341
00:45:00,250 --> 00:45:03,560
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

1342
00:45:03,850 --> 00:45:07,630
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

1343
00:45:10,110 --> 00:45:15,590
♫Every step we take has a meaning♫

1344
00:45:17,340 --> 00:45:22,040
♫No path is ever meaningless♫

1345
00:45:24,520 --> 00:45:30,660
♫As long as our hearts keep searching♫

1346
00:45:31,570 --> 00:45:36,140
♫One day, we'll find
what we're yearning for♫

1347
00:45:36,160 --> 00:45:39,670
♫Walking alone is fine,
but it's better when you're by my side♫

1348
00:45:39,690 --> 00:45:43,270
♫It won't be lonely
when you're here to walk beside♫

1349
00:45:43,290 --> 00:45:46,810
♫Like a love that waits, waits at the D Dorm♫

1350
00:45:46,830 --> 00:45:49,180
♫Like a love that remains,
remains at the dorm♫

1351
00:45:49,210 --> 00:45:55,530
♫Meaningful love and good things
await on every path♫

1352
00:45:56,190 --> 00:46:02,920
♫It might not be a coincidence
that we get to meet♫

1353
00:46:03,400 --> 00:46:10,550
♫There might be hidden meanings
on the path beneath our feet♫

1354
00:46:10,570 --> 00:46:17,490
♫Perhaps the D Dorm
is what led me to meet you♫

1355
00:46:17,510 --> 00:46:21,360
[The D Dorm]
